INSERT INTO `reading_passages` VALUES (1,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The shift toward remote work has transformed the modern business landscape significantly over the past few years. Companies of all sizes are discovering that allowing employees to work from home increases overall productivity and boosts job satisfaction. Furthermore, businesses can reduce their overhead costs by maintaining smaller physical office spaces. However, managing a remote team presents unique challenges for management. Communication can sometimes become fragmented, and maintaining a cohesive company culture requires intentional effort from team leaders. To overcome these hurdles, successful organizations invest in advanced collaboration tools and establish clear daily routines. Ultimately, flexibility has become a key factor in attracting top talent in a competitive job market, proving that remote work is more than just a temporary trend.','2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(2,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Business','B2','The modern business world is undergoing a significant transformation. Over the past few years, remote work has evolved from a temporary solution into a permanent business strategy for many companies. Organizations across various industries now allow their employees to work from home or any location of their choice. This shift offers numerous benefits, such as reduced operational costs for office space and increased employee satisfaction due to better work-life balance. Employers also report a broader talent pool, as they are no longer restricted by geographic boundaries when hiring new staff. However, managing a remote team comes with its own set of challenges. Maintaining effective communication and ensuring strong team collaboration can be difficult without face-to-face interaction. Furthermore, managers often worry about tracking employee productivity accurately. To overcome these obstacles, companies are heavily investing in digital collaboration tools like video conferencing software and project management applications. Ultimately, businesses that successfully balance flexibility with accountability will thrive in this new environment.','2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(3,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The modern business world is undergoing a significant transformation, driven largely by the rapid adoption of remote work policies. Companies of all sizes are discovering that employees can maintain high levels of productivity without being physically present in a traditional office environment. This shift offers numerous advantages, including reduced overhead costs for office space and greater flexibility for staff members. However, managing a remote workforce also presents unique challenges. Business leaders must find effective ways to maintain strong communication and build team cohesion when face-to-face interactions are limited. Furthermore, ensuring data security across multiple home networks requires substantial investment in advanced technology. Despite these obstacles, many organizations believe that hybrid models, which combine remote and in-office days, represent the future of work. By balancing flexibility with collaboration, companies can attract top talent from a global labor pool while keeping operational expenses manageable.','2026-09-14 23:36:32','2026-09-14 23:36:32'),(4,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','In recent years, the business world has witnessed a massive shift toward remote work. Driven by rapid technological advancements, many companies now allow employees to work from home or any location of their choice. This flexibility has significantly changed traditional office dynamics. Studies show that remote employees often experience higher productivity levels because they save time on daily commuting and enjoy a quieter work environment. Furthermore, businesses benefit by reducing overhead costs related to renting large office spaces and maintaining physical facilities. However, managing a remote team also presents distinct challenges. Communication can sometimes become fragmented, and managers find it harder to monitor daily progress without face-to-face interaction. To overcome these obstacles, successful organizations invest in advanced collaboration software like Slack and Zoom. Ultimately, remote work is no longer just a temporary trend; it has become a permanent strategy for modern enterprises striving to attract top global talent and retain satisfied workers.','2026-09-14 23:36:41','2026-09-14 23:36:41'),(5,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The modern business world is undergoing a significant transformation as more companies adopt remote work policies. Driven by rapid advancements in communication technology, organizations now allow employees to complete their tasks from home. This shift offers several notable advantages for both employers and staff members. For businesses, operating a virtual team significantly reduces overhead costs related to renting large office spaces and maintaining physical infrastructure. Meanwhile, employees enjoy a better work-life balance because they eliminate daily commuting stress and save valuable time. However, managing a remote workforce also presents distinct challenges. Managers often find it difficult to monitor productivity levels accurately and maintain strong team cohesion when colleagues never meet in person. To overcome these obstacles, successful companies implement daily virtual meetings and utilize specialized project management software. As a result, remote work is no longer just a temporary trend but a permanent strategy for many enterprises.','2026-09-14 23:36:49','2026-09-14 23:36:49'),(6,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Business','B2','The modern business world is undergoing a significant transformation, driven largely by the rapid adoption of remote work. Companies of all sizes are discovering that employees can be just as productive working from home as they are in a traditional office environment. This shift offers numerous benefits, including reduced overhead costs for office space and access to a broader, global talent pool. Furthermore, employees often report higher job satisfaction due to a better work-life balance and the elimination of daily commuting stress. However, managing a remote workforce also presents distinct challenges. Team leaders must find effective ways to maintain strong communication, build trust, and measure performance accurately without micromanaging. Cybersecurity is another major concern, as decentralized networks can expose corporate data to greater risks. Despite these hurdles, statistics show that hybrid and fully remote models are here to stay. Businesses that successfully adapt their management strategies to support remote employees will undoubtedly secure a competitive advantage in the future market.','2026-09-14 23:36:58','2026-09-14 23:36:58'),(7,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The modern business world is undergoing a significant transformation as more companies adopt remote work policies. Initially introduced as a temporary solution during global disruptions, working from home has now become a permanent strategy for many organizations. Research shows that remote employees often experience higher productivity levels and better work-life balance because they save valuable time on daily commutes. Furthermore, businesses benefit by reducing overhead costs associated with maintaining large physical office spaces and utilities. However, managing a remote team presents unique challenges for leadership. Communication can sometimes become fragmented, and maintaining a strong company culture requires deliberate effort from managers. To address these issues, successful companies now rely on specialized digital tools for project tracking and daily communication. Ultimately, flexibility has emerged as a crucial factor in attracting and retaining top talent in a competitive global market, making remote work a lasting pillar of contemporary corporate strategy.','2026-09-14 23:37:07','2026-09-14 23:37:07'),(8,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The COVID-19 pandemic permanently changed how companies operate, with remote work shifting from a temporary emergency measure to a permanent business strategy. Organizations across the globe discovered that employees can maintain high productivity levels while working from home. This flexibility has significantly reduced overhead costs for office space and utilities. Furthermore, businesses no longer face geographic limitations when hiring, allowing them to recruit top talent from anywhere in the world. However, managing remote teams presents distinct challenges. Communication can become fragmented, and maintaining a unified company culture is often difficult without face-to-face interaction. To address these issues, successful companies now invest in advanced digital collaboration tools and establish clear performance metrics rather than simply monitoring hours worked. Ultimately, the future of work belongs to organizations that can successfully balance employee flexibility with effective operational control, creating a sustainable model for long-term growth.','2026-09-14 23:37:15','2026-09-14 23:37:15'),(9,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The global business landscape has experienced a significant shift toward remote work over the past few years. Companies of all sizes now allow employees to work from home or other locations outside the traditional office. This transition offers several distinct advantages for both employers and staff members. For businesses, offering remote work options helps reduce overhead costs related to renting large office spaces and maintaining physical facilities. Furthermore, organizations can access a broader talent pool without geographic limitations. For workers, eliminating daily commuting saves valuable time and reduces stress. However, managing remote teams also presents unique challenges. Maintaining effective communication and ensuring data security are primary concerns for managers. Without proper tools and clear policies, productivity can decline. Therefore, modern enterprises must invest in robust digital infrastructure to support their distributed workforce effectively.','2026-09-14 23:37:23','2026-09-14 23:37:23'),(10,'business','The Rise of Remote Work in Modern Business','B2','The shift toward remote work has transformed the modern business landscape significantly over the past few years. Companies of all sizes are discovering that allowing employees to work from home can lead to higher productivity and increased job satisfaction. Furthermore, businesses can reduce their overhead costs by leasing smaller office spaces or eliminating them entirely. However, managing a remote workforce also presents unique challenges. Team leaders often struggle with communication gaps and maintaining a strong company culture when staff members are scattered across different locations. Additionally, ensuring data security becomes much more complex when employees access company networks from personal home Wi-Fi connections. To overcome these obstacles, successful organizations invest in collaborative software tools and establish clear daily guidelines. Ultimately, finding the right balance between flexibility and structure is essential for long-term success in a remote work environment.','2026-09-14 23:37:31','2026-09-14 23:37:31'),(11,'environment','The Impact of Urban Green Spaces','B2','Urban green spaces, such as parks and community gardens, play a vital role in modern cities. These natural areas improve air quality by absorbing pollutants and releasing oxygen. Moreover, trees and vegetation help reduce the urban heat island effect, which makes city centers significantly warmer than surrounding rural areas. In addition to environmental benefits, green spaces offer remarkable mental health advantages for urban residents. Studies show that spending time outdoors lowers stress levels and encourages physical activity, leading to a healthier population. Local governments are now investing more funds into creating these ecological zones. City planners design rooftop gardens and plant thousands of trees along busy streets to protect biodiversity. However, rapid urbanization threatens existing parks as land demand for residential buildings increases. Protecting these natural zones requires strict regulations and active community participation to ensure sustainable development for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:37:40','2026-09-14 23:37:40'),(12,'environment','The Rise of Urban Rooftop Farming','B2','Urban rooftop farming is becoming a popular solution for sustainable city living. As urban populations grow rapidly, traditional agriculture struggles to meet the high demand for fresh produce while reducing carbon emissions caused by long-distance transportation. Transforming concrete roofs into green spaces allows local communities to grow vegetables directly where they are consumed. These agricultural rooftops offer significant environmental benefits. They absorb massive amounts of rainwater, which effectively reduces the risk of urban flooding during heavy storms. Furthermore, plants on roofs help cool down buildings naturally by absorbing sunlight, decreasing the reliance on electricity-powered air conditioning. This reduction in energy consumption directly lowers greenhouse gas emissions from power plants. Despite these clear advantages, establishing a rooftop farm requires careful planning. Building owners must ensure the structure can support the heavy weight of soil, water, and mature plants. Waterproofing is also critical to prevent costly leaks. Nevertheless, cities around the world are investing heavily in this green movement because it transforms unused spaces into productive ecosystems that improve both public health and environmental quality.','2026-09-14 23:37:48','2026-09-14 23:37:48'),(13,'environment','The Impact of Urban Green Spaces','B2','Urban green spaces, such as parks and community gardens, play a vital role in modern cities. These natural areas improve air quality by absorbing pollutants and releasing oxygen. Moreover, trees and vegetation help reduce the urban heat island effect, making cities cooler during summer months. Beyond environmental benefits, parks provide residents with spaces for physical activity and social interaction, which significantly enhances mental well-being and reduces stress levels. However, as cities grow rapidly, these green areas face constant threats from real estate development and construction projects. Protecting urban nature requires careful city planning and strong local policies. City councils must invest in planting more trees and maintaining existing parks to ensure sustainable urban development for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:37:56','2026-09-14 23:37:56'),(14,'environment','The Impact of Urban Green Spaces','B2','Urban green spaces play a crucial role in improving the quality of life in modern cities. Parks and botanical gardens provide residents with essential areas for recreation and physical exercise, which contributes significantly to public health. Furthermore, trees and vegetation act as natural air filters. They absorb carbon dioxide and reduce harmful pollutants, leading to cleaner air for city dwellers. Urban greenery also helps mitigate the urban heat island effect by providing shade and cooling the surrounding environment through evapotranspiration. In addition to environmental and health benefits, well-maintained parks support local biodiversity by offering habitats for various bird and insect species. Despite these clear advantages, rapid urban development often threatens existing green areas as concrete buildings replace natural habitats. City planners must prioritize the preservation and expansion of urban forests to ensure sustainable and resilient cities for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:38:05','2026-09-14 23:38:05'),(15,'environment','The Impact of Urban Green Spaces','B2','Urban green spaces, such as parks and community gardens, play a vital role in modern cities. These natural areas improve air quality by absorbing pollutants and producing oxygen. Furthermore, trees and vegetation help reduce the urban heat island effect, making city temperatures more manageable during hot summer months. Beyond environmental benefits, parks provide significant mental health advantages for residents. Regular access to nature has been proven to lower stress levels and encourage physical activity among people of all ages. City planners are now prioritizing the development of green rooftops and vertical gardens to maximize limited space. However, maintaining these areas requires a consistent supply of water and financial resources from local governments. Despite these challenges, investing in urban nature is essential for creating sustainable and livable cities for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:38:13','2026-09-14 23:38:13'),(16,'environment','Urban Greening Initiatives','B2','Urban greening initiatives are transforming modern cities across the globe. As populations grow, concrete structures replace natural landscapes, leading to higher temperatures and increased air pollution. To combat these issues, city planners are introducing more parks, rooftop gardens, and vertical forests. These green spaces do more than just beautify urban areas; they provide vital ecological benefits. Plants absorb carbon dioxide and release oxygen, which significantly improves air quality. Furthermore, vegetation helps lower ambient temperatures by providing shade and cooling the surrounding air through a process called evapotranspiration. Research shows that residents living near green areas experience lower stress levels and are more physically active. Despite these clear advantages, funding remains a major challenge for local governments. Maintenance costs and limited space in densely populated districts often delay the implementation of new environmental projects. However, community involvement has proven effective in overcoming some of these financial hurdles. Volunteers often help plant trees and maintain local parks, ensuring that urban centers remain sustainable and livable for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:38:21','2026-09-14 23:38:21'),(17,'environment','The Impact of Urban Green Spaces','B2','Urban green spaces, such as public parks and rooftop gardens, play a vital role in modern cities. As urban areas expand rapidly, natural habitats are destroyed, leading to higher temperatures and increased pollution. Planting trees and creating gardens help combat the urban heat island effect by providing shade and cooling the air through transpiration. Furthermore, vegetation absorbs carbon dioxide and filters harmful pollutants from the atmosphere, significantly improving air quality for city residents. Beyond environmental benefits, these green areas offer important social and psychological advantages. Studies show that spending time in nature reduces stress levels, encourages physical activity, and fosters a sense of community among neighbors. City planners are now prioritizing the integration of sustainable ecosystems into urban designs. By converting abandoned lots into community gardens and requiring green roofs on new buildings, municipalities can protect local wildlife and enhance the overall well-being of the population. Investing in urban nature is no longer optional; it is a necessity for sustainable development.','2026-09-14 23:38:30','2026-09-14 23:38:30'),(18,'environment','Urban Greening Initiatives','B2','Urban greening initiatives are transforming modern cities by integrating nature into dense concrete landscapes. City planners are increasingly planting native trees, creating rooftop gardens, and establishing community parks to combat environmental challenges. One major benefit is the reduction of the urban heat island effect, which occurs when cities absorb and trap heat due to dark surfaces like asphalt and roofs. Furthermore, green spaces significantly improve air quality by filtering pollutants and absorbing carbon dioxide. They also manage stormwater runoff effectively, absorbing rainwater and reducing the risk of urban flooding. Beyond environmental advantages, these natural areas provide substantial mental health benefits for residents. Access to parks lowers stress levels and encourages physical activity, leading to healthier communities. However, maintaining these urban ecosystems requires careful water management and continuous financial investment from local governments. Despite these challenges, green cities represent a sustainable approach to urban development, ensuring that nature and infrastructure coexist harmoniously for future generations.','2026-09-14 23:38:39','2026-09-14 23:38:39'),(19,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','My name is Anna, and I live in a small town. Every weekend, I like to relax and spend time with my family. On Saturday morning, I wake up at eight o\'clock. First, I make a cup of hot coffee and eat toast with butter for breakfast. Then, my husband and I go to the local market to buy fresh vegetables and fruit. In the afternoon, we usually clean the house together. My daughter helps me wash the dishes, and my son cleans his bedroom. On Sunday, we do something fun. Sometimes we visit my parents who live in the countryside. Other times, we go to the public park for a long walk. When the weather is very hot, we sit under the green trees and read books. In the evening, we watch a nice movie together in the living room. I always feel happy and ready for work when Monday morning arrives.','2026-09-14 23:38:47','2026-09-14 23:38:47'),(20,'general','A Day at the Local Market','A2','Every Saturday morning, Anna goes to the local outdoor market in her neighborhood. She likes to buy fresh fruit and vegetables for the coming week. The market is always busy and noisy, but the atmosphere is very friendly. First, she visits her favorite fruit stall to buy sweet red apples and juicy oranges. The friendly vendor always gives her a free banana to taste. After that, Anna walks to the vegetable section to choose green broccoli, carrots, and onions. Everything at the market is much cheaper and fresher than the food at the big supermarkets. Before going home, she usually stops by a small bakery to buy a warm loaf of bread for breakfast. Shopping at the market takes about one hour, but Anna always enjoys this peaceful morning routine.','2026-09-14 23:38:55','2026-09-14 23:38:55'),(21,'general','The Benefits of Walking','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and most popular forms of exercise in the world. You do not need expensive equipment or a special gym membership to start walking. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes and some free time. Regular walking can help you stay healthy and strong. It is very good for your heart and can help you maintain a healthy weight. Many people like to walk in the morning before they go to work because it gives them more energy for the day. Others prefer to walk in the evening to relax after a stressful day at the office. Walking with a friend or a family member is also a great way to talk and spend quality time together. Even a short walk of twenty minutes every day can make a big difference in your physical and mental health. Therefore, taking a walk daily is a simple habit that everyone should try to build.','2026-09-14 23:39:03','2026-09-14 23:39:03'),(22,'general','The Rise of Urban Farming','B2','Urban farming is becoming increasingly popular in major cities around the world. As urban populations grow, more people are looking for sustainable ways to access fresh produce. City residents are transforming rooftop spaces, balconies, and abandoned lots into thriving vegetable gardens. This movement not only provides fresh food but also helps reduce the carbon footprint associated with transporting groceries over long distances. Furthermore, community gardens offer a wonderful opportunity for neighbors to connect and learn gardening skills together. Despite challenges such as limited sunlight and restricted space, innovative techniques like vertical farming and hydroponics are helping growers achieve great success. Local governments are beginning to support these initiatives by offering grants and organizing workshops for interested citizens. Ultimately, urban agriculture is transforming concrete jungles into green, sustainable communities.','2026-09-14 23:39:11','2026-09-14 23:39:11'),(23,'general','The Evolution of Urban Commuting','C1','Modern urban commuting has undergone a remarkable transformation over the past decade. As metropolitan areas expand and population density surges, traditional modes of transportation are increasingly strained. Municipal authorities are consequently compelled to rethink public transit infrastructure to reduce congestion and carbon emissions. One prominent strategy involves the widespread implementation of dedicated bicycle lanes, which encourage active travel and improve safety for cyclists. Furthermore, the proliferation of dockless electric scooters has provided a viable solution for the persistent first-mile and last-mile connectivity challenge. Commuters can now seamlessly bridge the gap between their residences and mass transit stations without relying on private automobiles. Nevertheless, this rapid integration of micro-mobility devices has not been without friction. Pedestrian safety concerns have escalated, prompting city planners to establish stricter parking regulations and speed limits for rental scooters. Ultimately, achieving a sustainable urban transport ecosystem requires a delicate balance between encouraging technological innovation and safeguarding public welfare in densely populated environments.','2026-09-14 23:39:20','2026-09-14 23:39:20'),(24,'health','The Benefits of Regular Physical Activity','B2','Regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing chronic diseases. Engaging in moderate exercise, such as brisk walking, cycling, or swimming, for at least thirty minutes a day can significantly improve cardiovascular health. Exercise helps strengthen the heart muscle, lowers blood pressure, and improves blood circulation throughout the body. Additionally, physical activity plays a crucial role in weight management by burning excess calories and boosting the metabolism. Beyond physical benefits, working out regularly has a positive impact on mental health. It triggers the release of endorphins, which are natural chemicals in the brain that reduce stress, anxiety, and symptoms of depression. Furthermore, active individuals often experience better sleep quality, waking up feeling more refreshed and energized. Experts recommend incorporating a mix of aerobic exercises and strength training into weekly routines for optimal health outcomes. Even small changes, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator, can make a noticeable difference over time.','2026-09-14 23:39:39','2026-09-14 23:39:39'),(25,'health','The Benefits of Regular Physical Activity','B2','Regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing chronic diseases. Engaging in moderate exercise, such as brisk walking, cycling, or swimming, for at least thirty minutes a day can significantly improve cardiovascular health. Exercise strengthens the heart muscle, lowers blood pressure, and helps regulate body weight by burning calories efficiently. In addition to physical benefits, working out plays a crucial role in mental well-being. Physical activity stimulates the release of endorphins, which are chemicals in the brain that act as natural mood lifters. This process helps reduce stress, anxiety, and symptoms of depression. Furthermore, consistent physical exertion improves sleep quality, allowing the body to recover and restore energy levels overnight. Despite these clear advantages, many people struggle to maintain a consistent routine due to busy schedules and sedentary habits. To overcome this challenge, experts recommend incorporating small changes into daily life, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator or going for a short walk during lunch breaks. By making these minor adjustments, individuals can gradually build a sustainable and healthy fitness habit.','2026-09-14 23:39:47','2026-09-14 23:39:47'),(26,'health','The Benefits of Daily Walking','B2','Regular physical activity is essential for maintaining good health and preventing chronic illnesses. Among various exercises, brisk walking is one of the most accessible and effective options for people of all ages. Walking for just thirty minutes a day can significantly improve cardiovascular health by strengthening the heart and lowering blood pressure. Furthermore, it helps maintain a healthy body weight and reduces the risk of developing type 2 diabetes. In addition to physical benefits, walking also has a positive impact on mental well-being. Outdoor walks expose individuals to natural sunlight and fresh air, which helps reduce daily stress, elevate mood, and boost energy levels. Unlike high-impact workouts, walking places minimal stress on the joints, making it a safe choice for older adults and beginners. Incorporating this simple habit into your daily routine requires no special equipment or gym membership, making it a convenient way to achieve a healthier lifestyle.','2026-09-14 23:39:55','2026-09-14 23:39:55'),(27,'health','The Benefits of Regular Physical Activity','B2','Regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing chronic diseases. Engaging in moderate exercise, such as brisk walking, cycling, or swimming, for at least thirty minutes a day can significantly improve cardiovascular health. Exercise strengthens the heart muscle, lowers blood pressure, and helps maintain a healthy body weight by burning calories efficiently. In addition to physical benefits, working out regularly has a profound impact on mental well-being. Physical activity triggers the release of endorphins, which are chemicals in the brain that act as natural painkillers and mood elevators. Consequently, people who exercise consistently report lower levels of stress, anxiety, and depression. Furthermore, regular movement improves sleep quality, allowing the body to recover and function at its best during the day. However, it is crucial to start slowly and consult a doctor before beginning any intense fitness program to avoid injuries. Incorporating small habits, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator, can make a noticeable difference in overall health over time.','2026-09-14 23:40:11','2026-09-14 23:40:11'),(28,'health','The Benefits of Regular Physical Activity','B2','Regular physical activity plays a vital role in maintaining overall health and preventing chronic illnesses. Engaging in at least 150 minutes of moderate aerobic exercise every week can significantly improve cardiovascular health, strengthen muscles, and boost mental well-being. Activities such as brisk walking, cycling, and swimming are excellent choices for people of all ages. Exercise also helps regulate body weight and reduces the risk of developing type 2 diabetes. Furthermore, physical movement releases endorphins, which are natural chemicals in the brain that elevate mood and reduce stress levels. Despite these proven benefits, many adults fail to meet the recommended activity guidelines due to busy schedules and sedentary jobs. Incorporating small changes, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator or walking during lunch breaks, can make a substantial difference in daily fitness levels.','2026-09-14 23:40:20','2026-09-14 23:40:20'),(29,'health','The Benefits of Regular Physical Activity','B2','Regular physical activity is essential for maintaining a healthy lifestyle and preventing chronic diseases. Engaging in moderate exercise, such as brisk walking, cycling, or swimming, for at least thirty minutes a day can significantly improve cardiovascular health. Exercise helps strengthen the heart muscle, lowers blood pressure, and reduces the risk of developing heart conditions. In addition to physical health benefits, working out plays a crucial role in mental well-being. Physical activity stimulates the release of endorphins, which are natural chemicals in the brain that elevate mood and reduce stress. Furthermore, consistent exercise improves the quality of sleep, allowing the body to recover and maintain high energy levels throughout the day. Despite these clear advantages, many individuals struggle to maintain a daily routine due to busy work schedules. Experts recommend starting with small steps, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator or going for a short walk during lunch breaks. By making these minor adjustments, people can gradually build a sustainable fitness habit that supports long-term health and vitality.','2026-09-14 23:40:31','2026-09-14 23:40:31'),(30,'history','The Rise of Alexandria','B2','Founded by Alexander the Great in 331 BC, Alexandria quickly became one of the most important cities of the ancient world. Located on the Mediterranean coast of Egypt, it served as a major strategic and commercial hub connecting Greece, the Middle East, and Africa. The city was world-famous for the Great Library of Alexandria, which aimed to gather all the knowledge in the world. Scholars from various regions traveled there to study, write, and conduct scientific research. Furthermore, Alexandria was home to the Pharos Lighthouse, one of the Seven Wonders of the Ancient World, which guided countless ships safely into its busy harbor. Despite experiencing numerous earthquakes, fires, and political conflicts over the centuries that destroyed many of its ancient structures, the cultural and historical legacy of Alexandria continues to fascinate modern historians and archaeologists today.','2026-09-14 23:40:48','2026-09-14 23:40:48'),(31,'history','The Rise of the Printing Press','B2','Before the invention of the mechanical movable-type printing press, books in Europe were painstakingly copied by hand by scribes, making them extremely rare and expensive. Only the wealthy elite and powerful religious institutions could afford to own them, and as a result, general literacy rates remained very low. Around 1440, Johannes Gutenberg, a German goldsmith and inventor, introduced his revolutionary printing press. By combining movable metal type with an oil-based ink and a modified wine press, Gutenberg made mass production of texts possible for the first time in European history. The first major book printed with his technology was the famous Gutenberg Bible in the 1450s. This incredible innovation drastically reduced the cost of book production and accelerated the spread of scientific, political, and religious ideas across the continent. Scholars agree that the printing press played a fundamental role in triggering the Renaissance and the Scientific Revolution.','2026-09-14 23:41:21','2026-09-14 23:41:21'),(32,'science','The Secrets of Sleep','B2','Sleep is a vital biological process that allows the human body and brain to recover from daily activities. During a normal night, humans cycle through several stages of sleep, including light sleep, deep sleep, and REM (Rapid Eye Movement) sleep. Deep sleep is particularly important because it is the phase when the body repairs tissues, builds bone and muscle, and strengthens the immune system. Meanwhile, REM sleep is essential for cognitive functions such as memory consolidation, learning, and emotional regulation. Without sufficient rest, individuals often experience difficulty concentrating, slower reaction times, and mood swings. Chronic sleep deprivation can even lead to serious health issues, including obesity, heart disease, and diabetes. Scientists generally recommend that healthy adults get between seven and nine hours of quality sleep every night to maintain optimal physical and mental performance. Unfortunately, modern lifestyles, stress, and screen time often disrupt these natural patterns, leaving many people chronically exhausted.','2026-09-14 23:42:27','2026-09-14 23:42:27'),(33,'health','The Power of Daily Walking','B2','Walking is one of the simplest and most effective forms of physical exercise to improve overall health. Research shows that walking for just thirty minutes a day can significantly reduce the risk of heart disease and type 2 diabetes. Furthermore, this low-impact activity helps strengthen bones, reduce excess body fat, and boost muscle power. Unlike running, walking does not put high pressure on joints, making it an ideal exercise for people of all ages and fitness levels. Beyond physical health benefits, daily walking also enhances mental well-being. Regular walks release endorphins, which are natural chemicals in the brain that lower stress levels and improve mood. Experts suggest walking outdoors in green spaces, such as public parks, to maximize these emotional benefits. To start, a person only needs a pair of comfortable walking shoes. No expensive gym memberships or specialized equipment are required, making walking a highly accessible and affordable routine for everyone.','2026-09-14 23:47:54','2026-09-14 23:47:54'),(34,'health','The Power of Micro-breaks','B2','In today\'s fast-paced work environment, maintaining high productivity often comes at the expense of physical and mental health. Many office workers suffer from digital eye strain, back pain, and chronic fatigue due to prolonged sitting. Fortunately, a highly effective solution lies in taking regular micro-breaks. These are brief pauses lasting between thirty seconds and two minutes, which should be taken every thirty minutes. Scientific research shows that micro-breaks can significantly reduce stress and improve concentration levels. During these short intervals, individuals can easily stand up, gently stretch their arms, or look at a distant object to rest their eyes. Implementing this simple habit does not disrupt daily workflow; instead, it boosts overall energy and prevents repetitive strain injuries. Additionally, drinking a glass of water during these pauses helps maintain proper hydration. By consciously integrating micro-breaks into their daily routine, employees can protect their physical well-being and boost their long-term professional performance.','2026-09-14 23:48:14','2026-09-14 23:48:14'),(35,'history','The Rediscovery of Machu Picchu','B2','In July 1911, an American historian named Hiram Bingham arrived in Peru with an expedition team. His primary goal was to find Vilcabamba, the lost capital of the Inca Empire. Guided by a local farmer named Melchor Arteaga, Bingham climbed the steep, forest-covered slopes of the Andes mountains. On July 24, they reached a high ridge where they discovered an extraordinary ancient site. It was Machu Picchu, a spectacular 15th-century Inca citadel that had remained hidden from the Spanish conquistadors and the outside world for centuries. The stone structures were remarkably preserved, covered only by centuries of thick vegetation. Although Bingham was not the first outsider to visit the ruins, his extensive documentation and photographs brought global attention to the site. In 1913, the National Geographic Society dedicated an entire issue to Machu Picchu, sparking worldwide fascination. Today, this UNESCO World Heritage Site is recognized as one of the New Seven Wonders of the World, attracting hundreds of thousands of tourists annually who marvel at its advanced engineering and breathtaking mountaintop location.','2026-09-14 23:48:35','2026-09-14 23:48:35'),(36,'history','The Discovery of the Rosetta Stone','B2','In 1799, during Napoleon Bonaparte’s military campaign in Egypt, French soldiers made an extraordinary discovery. While building fortifications near the port city of Rashid, also known as Rosetta, they found a large granodiorite stone slab. This artifact, later named the Rosetta Stone, featured a decree issued in 196 BC on behalf of King Ptolemy V. What made this stone remarkably valuable to historians was the fact that the same decree was carved in three different scripts: Ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs, Demotic script, and Ancient Greek. Since Ancient Greek was a well-known language, scholars used it as a key to decipher the other two scripts. French scholar Jean-François Champollion spent years studying the text and finally announced that he had cracked the hieroglyphic code in 1822. This breakthrough allowed modern historians to read and understand the ancient texts of Egypt for the very first time, effectively unlocking thousands of years of Egyptian history. Today, the Rosetta Stone remains one of the most visited objects in the British Museum in London.','2026-09-14 23:48:55','2026-09-14 23:48:55'),(37,'history','Unlocking Ancient Secrets: The Rosetta Stone','B2','The Rosetta Stone is one of the most famous archaeological discoveries in history. In July 1799, French soldiers led by Pierre-François Bouchard found the stone slab while building fortifications near the Egyptian town of Rashid (Rosetta). Made of dark granodiorite, the stone contains three inscriptions of the same decree issued at Memphis in 196 BC. The three scripts used are Ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs, Demotic script, and Ancient Greek. Because it presented essentially the same text in all three scripts, the stone became the key to deciphering Egyptian hieroglyphs. This breakthrough was achieved in 1822 by the French scholar Jean-François Champollion. He compared the Greek text, which was easily read, with the mysterious Egyptian hieroglyphs. Today, the Rosetta Stone is kept in the British Museum in London, where it has been on public display since 1802. It remains one of the most visited objects in the museum, attracting millions of tourists every year who are fascinated by its historical significance.','2026-09-14 23:49:15','2026-09-14 23:49:15'),(38,'history','The Discovery of the Rosetta Stone','B2','In July 1799, during Napoleon Bonaparte’s Egyptian campaign, French soldiers made an extraordinary discovery near the port city of Rashid, also known as Rosetta. While constructing defensive fortifications, a young officer named Pierre-François Bouchard noticed a large black stone embedded in an old wall. This basalt slab, measuring about 112 centimeters high, contained three distinct bands of writing. Scholars soon realized the stone’s immense historical value. The same decree, issued in 196 BC by King Ptolemy V, was inscribed in three different scripts: Ancient Egyptian hieroglyphs, Demotic script, and Ancient Greek. Because Ancient Greek was well known to historians, the stone provided the essential key to deciphering Egyptian hieroglyphs, which had been unreadable for centuries. In 1801, British forces defeated the French in Egypt and seized the stone under the Treaty of Alexandria. It was transported to Portsmouth in February 1802 and was later placed in the British Museum, where it has remained on public display almost continuously ever since. Today, it is one of the most famous and visited objects in the museum.','2026-09-14 23:49:31','2026-09-14 23:49:31'),(39,'history','The Invention that Shaped Modern History','B2','In the mid-15th century, a German goldsmith named Johannes Gutenberg introduced a revolutionary technology to Europe: the movable type printing press. Before this invention, books were painstakingly copied by hand, a process that took months or even years. Consequently, books were extremely rare and expensive, which limited formal education mostly to the wealthy elite and the clergy. Gutenberg’s press changed everything by allowing the mass production of texts for the first time. His most famous creation, the Gutenberg Bible, was completed around 1455 and marked the official beginning of the \'Gutenberg Revolution\'. The rapid spread of printing technology across Europe facilitated the sharing of new scientific, political, and religious ideas. This innovation played a crucial role in supporting major historical movements, including the Renaissance, the Protestant Reformation, and the Scientific Revolution. By making information widely accessible to the general public, Gutenberg\'s press laid the essential foundation for our modern knowledge-based society, permanently altering the course of human civilization.','2026-09-14 23:49:48','2026-09-14 23:49:48'),(40,'history','The Invention that Changed the World','B2','In the mid-15th century, a German goldsmith named Johannes Gutenberg introduced a revolutionary technology to Europe: the movable type printing press. Before this invention, books in Europe were painstakingly copied by hand, a process that took months or even years. This made books extremely rare and expensive, meaning only the wealthy and the clergy could afford them. Gutenberg\'s machine, which used metal alloy types and oil-based ink, allowed for the rapid mass production of written texts. By 1455, Gutenberg demonstrated the power of his invention by printing his famous 42-line Bible. The sudden availability of cheap, printed materials sparked a dramatic increase in literacy rates across the continent. It also facilitated the rapid spread of scientific, political, and religious ideas, directly fueling the Renaissance and the Scientific Revolution. Ultimately, the printing press democratized knowledge, transforming European society from an illiterate oral culture into an information-driven civilization.','2026-09-14 23:50:04','2026-09-14 23:50:04'),(41,'science','The Mystery of Bioluminescence','B2','Deep below the ocean surface, where sunlight cannot penetrate, many marine organisms have developed the ability to produce their own light. This fascinating natural phenomenon is known as bioluminescence. Unlike the light from a lightbulb, which generates a significant amount of heat, bioluminescence is a \'cold light\'. This means that less than 20% of the light produces heat, making it incredibly energy-efficient. Scientists have discovered that marine creatures use bioluminescence for several survival purposes. For instance, the anglerfish uses a glowing lure dangling above its mouth to attract curious prey. Other species, like certain types of jellyfish, flash bright lights to startle and scare away predators. Additionally, some deep-sea shrimp release a glowing cloud of chemicals into the water to temporarily blind their enemies, allowing them to escape safely into the dark. To generate this light, a chemical reaction must take place inside the organism. This reaction requires two main substances: a pigment called luciferin and an enzyme called luciferase. When luciferin reacts with oxygen, facilitated by the luciferase enzyme, light is produced. Understanding this unique chemical process has helped researchers develop new medical tools to track cellular activities inside the human body.','2026-09-14 23:50:24','2026-09-14 23:50:24'),(42,'science','The Glowing Secrets of the Deep Ocean','B2','Deep-sea bioluminescence is one of nature\'s most fascinating phenomena. In the dark depths of the ocean, where sunlight cannot penetrate, many marine organisms produce their own light through chemical reactions. This process involves a light-emitting molecule called luciferin and an enzyme known as luciferase. When these two substances react with oxygen, they release energy in the form of a bright glow, typically blue or green, because these colors travel best through seawater. Deep-sea creatures use this living light for various survival strategies. For instance, the anglerfish uses a glowing lure dangling from its head to attract unsuspecting prey. Other species, like certain types of squid, use bioluminescence for camouflage. By emitting light from their undersides, they match the faint light coming from the surface, making them invisible to predators swimming below them. Additionally, some organisms use sudden flashes of light to startle attackers, giving them a chance to escape. Understanding these deep-sea adaptations helps scientists develop new medical imaging technologies and biochemical sensors.','2026-09-14 23:50:45','2026-09-14 23:50:45'),(43,'science','The Glowing Ocean: Understanding Bioluminescence','B2','Bioluminescence is the production and emission of light by a living organism. It occurs widely in marine vertebrates and invertebrates, as well as in some fungi and insects. In the deep ocean, where sunlight cannot penetrate, bioluminescence serves as the primary source of light. Marine creatures use this natural glow for various essential survival strategies. One major function of bioluminescence is defense. Many species of deep-sea squid release a glowing cloud of chemical ink to distract predators, allowing them to escape into the darkness. Other creatures use bioluminescence for communication. For instance, some species of lanternfish emit specific light patterns to attract potential mates in the pitch-black waters. Furthermore, certain predators use light as a lure. The famous anglerfish has a glowing filament extending from its head, which attracts curious smaller fish directly to its mouth. This chemical reaction, which involves a light-emitting molecule called luciferin and an enzyme called luciferase, is highly efficient. Unlike human-made light bulbs, bioluminescence generates almost no heat, making it a \"cold light.\" Scientists are currently studying this efficiency to develop sustainable lighting technologies for human cities.','2026-09-14 23:51:03','2026-09-14 23:51:03'),(44,'science','Nature\'s Living Light','B2','Bioluminescence is the production and emission of light by a living organism. It occurs widely in marine vertebrates and invertebrates, as well as in some fungi, microorganisms, and terrestrial invertebrates. In the deep ocean, where sunlight cannot penetrate, bioluminescence is the primary source of light. Most deep-sea creatures produce blue-green light because these wavelengths travel easily through seawater. This biological light serves several critical survival purposes. First, organisms use it to attract prey. For instance, the anglerfish uses a glowing lure dangling from its head to draw smaller fish closer. Second, it is used for defense. When threatened, certain species of squid release a cloud of glowing ink to confuse predators and escape. Finally, bioluminescence plays a vital role in communication and mating. Fireflies, which are terrestrial insects, flash light patterns to find potential partners in the dark. Scientists are currently studying the chemical reactions behind this phenomenon to develop new medical technologies. They hope to use bioluminescent proteins as biosensors to detect diseases inside the human body.','2026-09-14 23:51:22','2026-09-14 23:51:22'),(45,'science','The Mystery of Deep-Sea Bioluminescence','B2','In the deepest parts of the ocean, where sunlight cannot reach, many marine organisms create their own light. This biological phenomenon, known as bioluminescence, is a chemical reaction that occurs inside the organism\'s body. To produce this cold light, two main substances are required: luciferin and luciferase. When luciferin reacts with oxygen, it produces a bright glow, often in shades of blue or green. Bioluminescence serves several crucial survival purposes. For instance, the anglerfish uses a glowing lure dangling in front of its head to attract prey in the pitch-black water. Other creatures, like certain species of jellyfish, use sudden flashes of bright light to startle and scare away predators. Additionally, some marine animals use specific light patterns to communicate with potential mates. Scientists are currently studying these glowing proteins to develop new medical imaging technologies. Understanding how these organisms generate light without heat could also help engineers create more energy-efficient lighting systems for human homes.','2026-09-14 23:51:40','2026-09-14 23:51:40'),(46,'science','Bioluminescence: Nature\'s Living Light','B2','Bioluminescence is the production and emission of light by a living organism. It occurs widely in marine vertebrates and invertebrates, as well as in some fungi and insects such as fireflies. In the deep ocean, where sunlight cannot penetrate, bioluminescence is crucial for survival. Organisms use this living light for various essential purposes, including luring prey, distracting predators, and communicating with potential mates. The chemical reaction that creates bioluminescence requires two unique substances: luciferin and luciferase. Luciferin is the compound that actually produces the light, while luciferase is an enzyme that accelerates the reaction. When oxygen combines with luciferin in the presence of luciferase, it releases energy in the form of a brilliant blue or green light. Because this process produces almost no heat, it is often referred to as cold light. Scientists are currently studying these chemical compounds to develop new medical imaging technologies and energy-efficient lighting systems for modern homes.','2026-09-14 23:52:01','2026-09-14 23:52:01'),(47,'science','Light in the Deep Ocean','B2','Bioluminescence is the production and emission of light by a living organism. It occurs widely in marine vertebrates and invertebrates, as well as in some fungi and microorganisms. In the deep ocean, where sunlight cannot penetrate, bioluminescence is the primary source of light. Creatures use this biological light for various survival purposes. For example, the deep-sea anglerfish uses a glowing lure dangling from its head to attract unsuspecting prey in the dark. Other species, like certain types of squid, eject a glowing cloud of bioluminescent chemical instead of dark ink to confuse predators and make a quick escape. Additionally, some jellyfish use sudden flashes of light to scare away potential threats or to signal to others of their species. Scientists study these remarkable organisms in their natural habitat using specialized submarines called submersibles. By understanding the chemical reactions that produce this unique cold light, researchers hope to develop new medical imaging technologies and energy-efficient lighting systems for human use in the near future.','2026-09-14 23:52:20','2026-09-14 23:52:20'),(48,'society','The Rise of Co-Living Spaces in Modern Cities','B2','In many major cities around the world, young professionals are embracing a new housing trend known as co-living. This housing concept involves residents sharing common areas like kitchens, living rooms, and workspaces, while maintaining their own private bedrooms. The primary driver behind this movement is the rapidly rising cost of urban housing, which makes renting traditional apartments unaffordable for many single adults. Beyond financial savings, co-living spaces offer a built-in community, effectively combating the urban loneliness that many newcomers experience in big cities. Property developers are quickly adapting to this demand by designing modern buildings specifically for communal living. These facilities often feature shared amenities such as fully equipped gyms, rooftop gardens, and high-speed internet, all included in a single monthly bill. Consequently, co-living is transforming from a temporary budget option into a preferred lifestyle choice for urban citizens who value social connection and convenience.','2026-09-14 23:52:48','2026-09-14 23:52:48'),(49,'society','The Rise of Urban Community Gardens','B2','In many modern cities, concrete landscapes are slowly being transformed by the rise of community gardens. These shared green spaces, managed collectively by local residents, offer far more than just fresh vegetables. They serve as vital social hubs that foster a strong sense of community and reduce urban isolation. A recent study in London revealed that eighty percent of participants felt less lonely after joining a local gardening project. These gardens provide a unique space where people of diverse backgrounds can meet and collaborate. Seniors share gardening tips with younger generations, while children learn about biology and nutrition firsthand. Moreover, community gardens contribute to environmental sustainability. They help lower local temperatures, support urban wildlife like bees, and reduce carbon emissions by promoting locally-grown food. However, maintaining these gardens requires ongoing volunteer commitment. Organizers often struggle to secure long-term funding and defend their green spaces against commercial property development. Despite these challenges, the social benefits of community gardens make them an invaluable asset to modern urban life.','2026-09-14 23:53:06','2026-09-14 23:53:06'),(50,'society','The Rise of Urban Community Gardens','B2','In recent years, urban community gardens have become increasingly popular in cities worldwide. These shared green spaces allow local residents to grow their own vegetables, fruits, and flowers. Beyond producing fresh food, these gardens serve a vital social purpose by bringing diverse groups of people together. Neighborhoods with community gardens often report a stronger sense of belonging and lower stress levels among residents. Volunteers of all ages collaborate on daily tasks, which helps bridge generational gaps. Many gardens also host educational workshops for children, teaching them about sustainability and healthy eating habits. However, establishing these gardens requires significant effort. Local organizers must secure land permissions from city councils and secure funding for essential tools. Despite these challenges, the social benefits of urban agriculture continue to inspire communities to transform vacant lots into vibrant, productive green spaces.','2026-09-14 23:53:20','2026-09-14 23:53:20'),(51,'society','The Rise of Co-housing Communities','B2','In recent years, co-housing has emerged as a popular housing alternative in many modern cities. Originating in Denmark in the 1960s, this living arrangement combines private homes with shared community spaces. Residents usually own their individual houses or apartments, but they share common facilities such as a large kitchen, dining room, gardens, and children\'s play areas. The primary goal of co-housing is to recreate a sense of neighborhood security and mutual support, which is often missing in busy urban environments. Members of these communities regularly organize shared meals and social events, fostering strong relationships among neighbors. Additionally, sharing resources like lawnmowers and laundry machines helps reduce living costs and promotes environmental sustainability. However, co-housing requires a high level of cooperation and active participation. Decision-making processes are usually democratic, meaning that all residents have a say in community rules. While this collaborative lifestyle might not appeal to everyone, it offers a practical solution to the growing problem of social isolation in modern society.','2026-09-14 23:57:15','2026-09-14 23:57:15'),(52,'technology','The Rise of Vertical Farming','B2','Vertical farming is transforming how we grow food in urban areas. Unlike traditional agriculture, which requires vast amounts of land, this technology allows crops to be grown in stacked layers inside controlled indoor environments. These high-tech facilities use artificial LED lights instead of sunlight and advanced hydroponic systems that deliver water and essential nutrients directly to the plant roots. One of the main advantages of vertical farming is its extreme efficiency. It uses up to 95 percent less water than conventional farming methods because the water is continuously recycled within the system. Furthermore, because the environment is completely sealed, crops are protected from harsh weather conditions and pests, eliminating the need for chemical pesticides. This ensures a reliable, year-round harvest of fresh vegetables. However, the technology does face some challenges. The initial setup cost for the specialized equipment and automated sensors is high. Additionally, vertical farms require a constant supply of electricity to power the climate control systems and LED lighting. Researchers are currently developing solar-powered systems to make vertical farming more sustainable and cost-effective for future generations.','2026-09-15 00:01:11','2026-09-15 00:01:11'),(53,'technology','The Rise of Smart Home Technology','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how we manage our daily household routines. By connecting appliances to the internet, these devices allow users to control heating, lighting, and security systems remotely. For instance, smart thermostats can learn a family\'s daily schedule to optimize energy consumption, which significantly reduces monthly electricity bills. Additionally, advanced security cameras now feature facial recognition technology, sending instant alerts to homeowners\' smartphones if an unrecognized person is detected on the property. Despite these convenient benefits, there are growing concerns regarding data privacy. Because smart devices constantly collect personal information, such as daily habits and voice recordings, they can be highly vulnerable to cyberattacks. Cybersecurity experts advise users to update their device software regularly and use strong, unique passwords for every connected appliance to prevent unauthorized access. In the near future, as the smart home market continues to expand rapidly, manufacturers will be pressured to implement much stronger encryption standards to protect sensitive consumer data from hackers.','2026-09-15 00:01:49','2026-09-15 00:01:49'),(54,'technology','The Rise of Smart Home Technology','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how we manage our households. By connecting appliances to the internet, these systems allow users to control heating, lighting, and security devices remotely using a smartphone app. One of the main benefits is energy efficiency. Smart thermostats, for example, can learn a family\'s daily routine and adjust the temperature automatically, which reduces electricity bills. Security is another major advantage; smart cameras send real-time alerts to homeowners if unexpected movement is detected inside the house. However, there are also challenges. Setting up these interconnected systems can be expensive, and they require a stable internet connection to function properly. Additionally, privacy remains a concern. Since smart devices collect personal data, they can sometimes be targeted by hackers. Despite these risks, the market for smart home devices continues to expand rapidly as manufacturers develop more secure and affordable products. Experts predict that within a decade, voice-activated assistants will be standard features in almost every modern household.','2026-09-15 00:02:07','2026-09-15 00:02:07'),(55,'technology','Smart Homes for a Greener Future','B2','Smart home technology is rapidly changing how we manage our daily lives and energy consumption. Modern smart thermostats, for instance, can learn a household\'s daily schedule and adjust temperatures automatically. This ensures that heating or cooling is only used when someone is actually at home, significantly reducing electricity bills. Additionally, smart lighting systems allow users to turn off forgotten lights remotely using a mobile application. Some advanced systems even utilize motion sensors to deactivate lights in empty rooms. Beyond convenience, these modern innovations play a crucial role in environmental conservation by minimizing unnecessary energy waste. Experts estimate that integrating smart devices can lower a household\'s carbon footprint by up to fifteen percent annually. Furthermore, smart water monitors can detect leaks early, preventing costly water damage and resource depletion. As these technologies become more affordable and easier to install, they are transitioning from expensive luxury items into essential tools for sustainable living.','2026-09-15 00:02:28','2026-09-15 00:02:28'),(56,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how people live by connecting everyday household devices to the internet. Homeowners can now control lighting, security cameras, and heating systems remotely using their smartphones or voice assistants. This technology offers significant benefits, particularly in energy conservation. For example, smart thermostats can automatically adjust indoor temperatures based on the residents\' daily routines, which reduces electricity bills significantly. Moreover, security systems send instant alerts to mobile phones if any unusual movement is detected, providing greater peace of mind for families. However, smart homes also present certain challenges. Cybersecurity is a major concern, as connected devices can potentially be hacked by malicious individuals if security protocols are weak. Additionally, the initial cost of purchasing and installing these advanced systems is often very high. Despite these drawbacks, the demand for smart home technology continues to grow rapidly worldwide as devices become more user-friendly and affordable.','2026-09-15 00:06:24','2026-09-15 00:06:24'),(57,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes. Today, homeowners can control various appliances and security systems using their smartphones or voice assistants. Devices like smart thermostats learn user preferences over time to adjust indoor temperatures automatically, which helps save energy and reduces monthly utility bills. Furthermore, advanced security cameras allow residents to monitor their property remotely while they are away at work or traveling. Although these innovations offer remarkable convenience and peace of mind, they also present potential risks. Cybersecurity threats are a growing concern because smart devices connect to the internet, making them vulnerable to hacking if security protocols are weak. Therefore, experts recommend using strong passwords and updating device software regularly to protect personal data from unauthorized access. As artificial intelligence continues to evolve, our homes will undoubtedly become even more intelligent and connected in the near future.','2026-09-15 00:10:38','2026-09-15 00:10:38'),(58,'technology','The Rise of Smart Home Technology','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how people live today. Modern devices allow homeowners to control lighting, security systems, and temperature remotely using smartphones. For example, intelligent thermostats can learn daily routines and adjust heating automatically to save energy. Security cameras provide live video feeds directly to users, increasing peace of mind. Although these systems offer great convenience, they also present potential risks. Cybersecurity threats are a major concern because hackers can exploit weak Wi-Fi networks to gain access to personal devices. Additionally, the high cost of installation prevents many families from adopting these innovations. Despite these challenges, the demand for connected homes continues to grow rapidly as manufacturers improve data protection and reduce prices.','2026-09-15 00:10:47','2026-09-15 00:10:47'),(59,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has completely changed how we live inside our houses. Smart home systems allow residents to control lighting, security cameras, and temperature using their smartphones. One of the main benefits of these connected devices is energy efficiency. For example, intelligent thermostats can learn daily routines and automatically adjust heating when nobody is home, which significantly reduces electricity bills. Furthermore, advanced security systems provide homeowners with real-time alerts if suspicious movement is detected around the property. However, this high level of connectivity also introduces potential risks. Experts warn that smart devices can be vulnerable to cyber attacks if users do not secure their home networks with strong passwords. Despite these security challenges, the global market for smart home technology continues to grow rapidly as more people seek convenience and safety in their daily lives.','2026-09-15 00:10:53','2026-09-15 00:10:53'),(60,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes. Today, homeowners can control lighting, security systems, and temperature using their smartphones or voice assistants. For example, smart thermostats learn daily routines and adjust heating automatically to save energy. Meanwhile, advanced security cameras send instant alerts to mobile devices whenever motion is detected outside. These automated systems offer incredible convenience and peace of mind for busy families. However, relying heavily on connected devices also presents privacy risks. Hackers might target weak Wi-Fi networks to gain access to personal data. Therefore, experts recommend using strong passwords and updating device software regularly to protect home networks against potential cyber threats.','2026-09-15 00:14:41','2026-09-15 00:14:41'),(61,'technology','The Rise of Smart Home Technology','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how people live by connecting household appliances to the internet. Homeowners can now control lighting, security systems, and heating remotely using smartphones or voice assistants. This automation offers significant benefits, particularly in energy conservation. For instance, smart thermostats learn daily routines and adjust temperatures automatically, reducing electricity bills. Furthermore, advanced security cameras provide real-time alerts to mobile phones, giving residents greater peace of mind whether they are at work or on vacation. Despite these advantages, some challenges remain. Cybersecurity is a major concern, as connected devices can be vulnerable to hacking if security protocols are weak. Additionally, the initial cost of purchasing and installing these gadgets can be expensive for average families. Nevertheless, market demand continues to grow rapidly as manufacturers make devices more affordable and user-friendly. As artificial intelligence advances further, future smart homes will likely become even more intuitive and integrated into daily routines.','2026-09-15 00:29:47','2026-09-15 00:29:47'),(62,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes. Today, homeowners can control lighting, security systems, and room temperature using their smartphones. Voice assistants like Alexa and Google Home allow users to manage devices simply by speaking commands. One of the main benefits of these connected systems is energy efficiency. Smart thermostats learn daily routines and adjust heating automatically, which significantly reduces electricity bills. Furthermore, advanced security cameras send instant alerts to mobile phones if they detect unusual movement outside the property. However, this high level of connectivity also brings potential risks. Cybersecurity threats are a growing concern because hackers could potentially access personal networks through vulnerable smart devices. To protect their privacy, experts strongly advise users to update their passwords regularly and secure their home Wi-Fi networks. As technology continues to evolve, smart homes will undoubtedly become even more integrated into our daily lives.','2026-09-15 00:30:02','2026-09-15 00:30:02'),(63,'technology','The Rise of Smart Home Technology','B2','Smart home technology has transformed how people manage their daily lives. Devices such as smart thermostats, automated lighting systems, and voice-activated assistants are becoming increasingly common in modern households. These technologies allow homeowners to control various appliances remotely using smartphones or tablets. One of the primary benefits of smart homes is energy efficiency. Smart thermostats can learn occupants\' schedules and adjust temperatures automatically to reduce power consumption. Furthermore, advanced security systems provide real-time alerts and video surveillance, giving residents greater peace of mind whether they are at home or away. However, integrating these systems can be challenging. Many users experience technical difficulties during the initial installation process. Additionally, privacy concerns regarding data collection by smart devices remain a significant issue for consumers. Despite these challenges, the demand for connected home devices continues to grow rapidly as manufacturers improve user interfaces and security protocols.','2026-09-15 00:30:08','2026-09-15 00:30:08'),(64,'society','Eaque illo nam occaecati qui.','B2','Sint voluptatem natus ipsam delectus maiores. Mollitia tempore totam asperiores enim dolores modi. Ea vel omnis distinctio repudiandae aut dolorem. Beatae quia quae sequi nemo sapiente autem quasi. Nemo quos libero vero minus quas. Odit ipsam sit quo inventore animi. Quia autem et error aliquam.','2026-09-15 00:39:49','2026-09-15 00:39:49'),(65,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes where everyday devices are connected to the internet. Homeowners can now control lighting, security cameras, and heating systems remotely using their smartphones. This automation not only increases convenience but also significantly improves energy efficiency. For instance, smart thermostats learn user habits and adjust temperatures automatically to reduce electricity waste. However, this high level of connectivity brings potential security risks. Hackers can potentially exploit vulnerabilities in smart devices to gain unauthorized access to private networks. Therefore, cybersecurity has become a top priority for tech companies developing these gadgets. As artificial intelligence continues to improve, future smart homes will become even more intuitive and secure.','2026-09-15 00:57:31','2026-09-15 00:57:31'),(66,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed how people live through the rise of smart home systems. These systems connect everyday household devices to the internet, allowing homeowners to control them remotely using smartphones or voice assistants. For instance, smart thermostats can automatically learn user temperature preferences and adjust heating schedules to save energy. Similarly, advanced security cameras provide real-time video alerts directly to mobile phones, giving residents greater peace of mind while they are away. Furthermore, smart lighting allows users to dim lights or change colors simply by using voice commands. Although these connected devices offer remarkable convenience and improve energy efficiency, they also present potential security risks. Hackers can potentially access home networks through vulnerable IoT devices if users fail to update their software regularly. Therefore, cybersecurity remains a major concern for manufacturers and consumers alike as smart home technology continues to evolve.','2026-09-15 00:57:45','2026-09-15 00:57:45'),(67,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','My name is Linh and I live in Hanoi. Every Sunday, I go to the big park near my house with my family. We usually wake up early at 7 AM. My mother makes delicious sandwiches and my father packs cold water and fresh fruit into a big basket. At the park, we love to walk on the green grass and listen to the birds singing in the tall trees. Sometimes, we rent a red bicycle and ride around the lake. My younger brother loves playing football with other children. In the afternoon, we sit under a large tree to eat our lunch and talk about our week. We always have a wonderful time together. We go back home at 5 PM because we are very tired but happy.','2026-09-15 11:43:30','2026-09-15 11:43:30'),(68,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','My name is Anna and I love weekends. On Saturday morning, I usually wake up at 8 o\'clock. I make a cup of hot coffee and eat toast with butter for breakfast. After breakfast, I clean my small apartment and wash my dirty clothes. In the afternoon, I go to the local supermarket to buy fresh vegetables, milk, and apples. I like cooking dinner for myself in the evening. I usually make chicken soup and rice. On Sunday, I like to relax. I visit my parents who live near my house. We talk, eat lunch together, and play board games in the living room. In the evening, I read an interesting book before I go to sleep. Weekends give me energy for a new week at work.','2026-09-15 11:43:38','2026-09-15 11:43:38'),(69,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','Every Saturday morning, Anna goes to the green park near her house. She likes to walk on the soft grass and look at the colorful flowers. Sometimes, she sits on a wooden bench to read her favorite book. At around ten o\'clock, children play football with their friends, and dogs run happily with red balls. Anna usually buys a cold bottle of orange juice from a small shop. The weather is always sunny and warm on these days. Anna thinks the park is a very peaceful and happy place to relax after a busy week of work.','2026-09-15 11:43:45','2026-09-15 11:43:45'),(70,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','Every Saturday, I wake up at 8 o\'clock in the morning. First, I make a cup of hot coffee and eat some toast with butter for breakfast. Then, I clean my small apartment and wash my clothes. In the afternoon, I usually go to the local supermarket to buy fresh vegetables, milk, and apples. Walking to the market helps me stay healthy and active. In the evening, I like to relax by reading a good book or watching a funny movie on TV. On Sunday, I visit my parents who live in the countryside. We always cook a delicious lunch together and talk about our week. Sometimes, we go for a walk in the green park near their house. Weekend is my favorite time of the week because I can rest and spend time with my family.','2026-09-15 11:43:53','2026-09-15 11:43:53'),(71,'general','My Morning Routine','A2','Every day, I wake up at six o\'clock in the morning. First, I wash my face and brush my teeth in the bathroom. Then, I go to the kitchen to prepare breakfast with my mother. We usually eat bread and eggs, and we drink a warm cup of coffee. After breakfast, I put on my school uniform and pack my bag. At seven-thirty, I walk to school with my best friend, Nam. Our classes start at eight o\'clock. In the afternoon, I come home at four o\'clock. I do my homework and help my parents clean the house before dinner. In the evening, I read books and watch television with my family. I go to sleep at ten o\'clock.','2026-09-15 11:44:00','2026-09-15 11:44:00'),(72,'general','A Day at the Local Market','A2','Every Saturday morning, Anna visits the local outdoor market in her neighborhood. She usually arrives at around 8 a.m. before it gets too crowded. The market is full of colorful stalls selling fresh fruits, vegetables, flowers, and handmade crafts. Anna always starts her trip by buying organic apples and ripe bananas from her favorite farmer, Mr. Brown. After that, she walks over to the bakery section to get a warm loaf of bread for breakfast. Sometimes, she also buys some red roses to decorate her living room table. Shopping at the market is much better than going to the supermarket because the food is fresher and the local people are very friendly. Anna loves talking to the vendors and hearing their stories. By 10 a.m., her shopping bags are heavy, and she happily walks back home to enjoy her fresh food.','2026-09-15 11:44:08','2026-09-15 11:44:08'),(73,'general','A Day at the Local Market','A2','Every Saturday morning, Maria goes to the local outdoor market to buy food for her family. The market opens at seven o\'clock, but Maria likes to arrive around eight to avoid the early morning crowd. She brings a large shopping bag made of cloth instead of using plastic bags. First, she walks to the fruit stall and buys fresh apples, bananas, and sweet oranges. The fruit vendor, an old man named David, always gives her a discount because she is a regular customer. Next, Maria visits the vegetable section to pick up green beans, carrots, and onions. After getting all the fresh ingredients, she stops by a small bakery to buy a loaf of warm bread for breakfast. Shopping at the local market is not only cheaper than going to the big supermarket, but the food is also much fresher. Maria enjoys talking to the friendly local sellers and always leaves the market with a smile on her face.','2026-09-15 11:44:16','2026-09-15 11:44:16'),(74,'general','A Day at the Local Market','A2','Every Saturday morning, Anna goes to the local market with her mother. The market is very busy and noisy, but Anna loves it. They always walk there because it is only ten minutes from their house. First, they buy fresh fruit like apples and bananas. Then, they go to the vegetable stall to get carrots, tomatoes, and green beans. Anna\'s favorite part is visiting the bakery. The baker always gives her a small piece of chocolate cake for free. After buying all the food, they carry heavy bags back home. In the afternoon, Anna helps her mother wash the vegetables and prepare a big lunch for the family. It is a simple routine, but it makes them very happy every weekend.','2026-09-15 11:44:23','2026-09-15 11:44:23'),(75,'general','The Benefits of Walking','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and most popular forms of exercise in the world. You do not need expensive equipment or a special gym membership to start walking. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes and some free time. Walking for just thirty minutes a day can greatly improve your physical and mental health. It helps keep your heart strong, builds muscle strength, and prevents weight gain. Moreover, walking outdoors allows you to breathe fresh air and enjoy nature, which is a great way to reduce daily stress and clear your mind after a long day at work or school. Many people like to walk with friends or family members, turning a healthy habit into an enjoyable social activity. Whether you walk quickly in the morning or take a slow stroll in the evening, this simple activity brings many long-term benefits to your life.','2026-09-15 11:44:31','2026-09-15 11:44:31'),(76,'general','The Benefits of Walking Daily','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and most effective ways to stay healthy. You do not need expensive equipment or a gym membership to start. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes and a little bit of free time every day. Taking a brisk walk for thirty minutes a day can greatly improve your physical and mental health. Physically, walking helps you control your weight, strengthens your bones, and keeps your heart healthy. Mentally, it is a great way to reduce stress after a long day at work or school. Many people like to listen to music or podcasts while walking in their local park. Another big advantage is that walking is suitable for people of all ages. Whether you are young or elderly, you can easily walk at your own pace. Therefore, making a daily walking habit is a wonderful choice for a better lifestyle.','2026-09-15 11:44:38','2026-09-15 11:44:38'),(77,'general','The Benefits of Walking','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and most popular ways to stay healthy. You do not need expensive equipment or a gym membership to start. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes. Walking for just thirty minutes a day can help you live a happier and healthier life. First, it strengthens your heart and reduces the risk of heart disease. Second, it helps you manage your weight by burning calories. When you walk outside, you also get fresh air and sunlight, which can improve your mood and reduce stress levels. Furthermore, walking is a great social activity. You can walk with your friends, family members, or neighbors while catching up on your daily news. If you prefer to be alone, it is a wonderful time to listen to your favorite music or a podcast. Therefore, adding a short daily walk to your routine is a simple choice with amazing benefits for both your body and mind.','2026-09-15 11:44:46','2026-09-15 11:44:46'),(78,'general','The Benefits of Walking','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and cheapest ways to stay healthy. You do not need expensive equipment or a gym membership to start. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes and some free time. Experts recommend walking for at least thirty minutes a day, five days a week. This simple habit can help you control your weight, strengthen your bones, and improve your mood. Moreover, walking outdoors allows you to enjoy nature and fresh air, which is great for reducing stress after a long day at work. Many people like to walk in the morning before breakfast to wake up their bodies. Others prefer walking in the evening to relax. If you live close to your workplace, you can even walk to work instead of driving. This not only saves money on gas but also helps protect the environment by reducing air pollution.','2026-09-15 11:44:54','2026-09-15 11:44:54'),(79,'general','The Rise of Urban Farming','B2','Urban farming is becoming increasingly popular in major cities around the world. Instead of transporting fresh produce over long distances, city residents are now growing vegetables and herbs in small spaces. Rooftops, balconies, and abandoned lots are being transformed into green spaces. This movement not only provides fresh food for local communities but also helps reduce carbon emissions from transportation. Furthermore, urban agriculture improves air quality and lowers the temperature in densely populated areas. Many schools and community centers have also started their own gardens to educate children about healthy eating and sustainability. While there are challenges such as limited sunlight and soil pollution, modern techniques like hydroponics make it easier than ever to grow plants without soil. As cities continue to expand, urban farming offers a practical solution to make our urban environments greener and more self-sufficient.','2026-09-15 11:45:01','2026-09-15 11:45:01'),(80,'general','The Benefits of Urban Gardening','B2','Urban gardening has become increasingly popular in many modern cities over the last decade. As more people move into apartments with limited outdoor space, residents are finding creative ways to grow their own food. Balconies, windowsills, and even shared community rooftops are now being transformed into green spaces filled with vegetables, herbs, and flowers. One major benefit of this trend is the improvement of mental health. Tending to plants helps reduce daily stress and encourages a sense of calm after a long day of work. Additionally, urban gardening provides fresh, organic produce right at home, which reduces grocery bills and minimizes plastic packaging waste. Furthermore, these green areas help lower urban temperatures by providing shade and absorbing less heat than concrete surfaces. City planners now actively support community garden projects because they bring neighbors together and strengthen social connections. Despite the challenges of limited sunlight and restricted space, urban agriculture continues to grow rapidly as city dwellers seek healthier and more sustainable lifestyles.','2026-09-15 11:45:10','2026-09-15 11:45:10'),(81,'general','The Rise of Urban Farming','B2','Urban farming is becoming increasingly popular in major cities around the world. As urban populations continue to grow, city residents are looking for innovative ways to grow their own food. Rooftop gardens, vertical farms, and community plots are transforming unused spaces into productive agricultural areas. This movement provides numerous benefits to local communities. First, growing food locally reduces the carbon footprint associated with transporting groceries over long distances. Second, fresh vegetables and fruits harvested directly from urban plots often contain higher nutrient levels than store-bought produce. Additionally, community gardening creates a strong sense of social connection among neighbors who work together to maintain the plots. Despite these advantages, urban gardeners face certain challenges, such as limited space and soil pollution from city traffic. To overcome these obstacles, many farmers now use advanced hydroponic systems that require no soil at all. Ultimately, urban farming is not just a passing trend; it is a vital step toward creating sustainable and resilient cities for future generations.','2026-09-15 11:45:17','2026-09-15 11:45:17'),(82,'general','The Rise of Urban Gardening','B2','Urban gardening has become increasingly popular in major cities around the world over the past decade. With limited green space available, city dwellers are finding creative ways to grow their own food. Rooftops, balconies, and even tiny windowsills are now transformed into productive vegetable patches. This trend offers numerous benefits for local communities. First, growing your own vegetables ensures access to fresh and organic produce without harmful pesticides. Second, taking care of plants is a proven way to reduce daily stress and improve mental well-being after a long day at work. Furthermore, local green spaces help lower urban temperatures during hot summer months and attract beneficial insects like bees and butterflies. Although starting a garden requires patience and basic knowledge, many urban residents agree that the effort is truly worthwhile. Local community centers often organize free workshops to teach beginners how to plant herbs and vegetables successfully in small containers.','2026-09-15 11:45:25','2026-09-15 11:45:25'),(83,'general','The Evolution of Urban Commuting','C1','Modern metropolitan areas face persistent challenges regarding traffic congestion and environmental degradation. To combat these issues, urban planners are increasingly prioritizing the development of robust micro-mobility infrastructure. Electric scooters and bicycles have transitioned from novelty items into indispensable modes of daily transit for millions of urban residents. This shift is primarily driven by the need to reduce carbon footprints and alleviate overcrowded public transportation networks. Commuters appreciate the flexibility and speed these compact vehicles offer during peak travel hours. However, integrating micro-mobility safely into existing road networks remains a significant hurdle. Municipalities must construct dedicated lanes to protect riders from vehicular traffic while simultaneously enforcing stricter parking regulations to prevent sidewalk clutter. Furthermore, technological advancements in battery efficiency continue to extend the operational range of these devices, making them even more viable for longer commutes. Ultimately, fostering a sustainable commuting culture requires continuous cooperation between city governments, transit operators, and everyday citizens who choose active transportation over private automobiles.','2026-09-15 11:45:33','2026-09-15 11:45:33'),(84,'general','The Evolution of Urban Commuting','C1','Modern urban commuting has undergone a remarkable transformation over the past decade. As cities expand and traffic congestion worsens, municipal authorities are increasingly prioritizing sustainable transport networks. Traditional reliance on private automobiles is steadily declining in metropolitan areas, replaced by an integrated mix of electric bicycles, efficient public transit, and pedestrian-friendly pathways. Furthermore, the implementation of dedicated bus lanes has drastically reduced travel times for daily commuters. Urban planners emphasize that reducing vehicular emissions is essential for achieving long-term environmental sustainability. Consequently, many cities have introduced bike-sharing schemes at affordable rates to encourage active mobility among residents. Despite these progressive initiatives, infrastructure challenges persist in densely populated districts where narrow streets limit the expansion of rapid transit networks. Addressing these spatial constraints requires innovative engineering solutions and substantial financial investment from both public and private sectors.','2026-09-15 11:45:41','2026-09-15 11:45:41'),(85,'general','The Evolution of Urban Commuting','C1','Modern urban commuting has undergone a profound transformation over the past decade. As metropolitan populations surge, municipal authorities face mounting pressure to alleviate severe traffic congestion and reduce carbon emissions. Traditional reliance on private automobiles is steadily declining in favor of integrated public transport networks and active mobility options. Electric scooters and bicycles, often available via dockless rental systems, have emerged as popular solutions for the final leg of a journey. Furthermore, dedicated bus rapid transit lanes and expanded subterranean rail networks offer commuters reliable alternatives to gridlocked streets. Urban planners emphasize that shifting commuter habits requires not only infrastructural investments but also psychological shifts regarding vehicle ownership. Ultimately, creating sustainable cities depends on our collective willingness to embrace flexible and shared transportation modes.','2026-09-15 11:45:49','2026-09-15 11:45:49'),(86,'general','The Evolution of Urban Commuting','C1','Modern urban commuting has undergone a remarkable transformation over the past decade. As cities expand and traffic congestion worsens, municipal authorities are increasingly prioritizing sustainable mobility solutions. Traditional reliance on private automobiles is steadily declining, replaced by a surge in active transportation methods such as cycling and walking. Furthermore, the integration of smart public transport networks has revolutionized daily travel. Commuters can now utilize real-time mobile applications to track bus schedules, rent electric scooters, and optimize their routes instantaneously. This technological shift not only reduces carbon emissions but also significantly enhances overall transit efficiency. However, challenges remain regarding infrastructure development and equitable access for all residents. Urban planners must continue to address these disparities to ensure that future transportation systems are both inclusive and environmentally friendly.','2026-09-15 11:45:57','2026-09-15 11:45:57'),(87,'society','The Rise of Remote Work','B2','In recent years, remote work has transformed modern society, altering how companies operate and how individuals manage their daily lives. Driven by advancements in digital technology, more employees now perform their professional duties from home instead of commuting to a traditional office. This shift offers significant benefits, such as a better work-life balance and the elimination of daily traffic stress. Employees save both time and money on transportation, while companies can access a global talent pool without geographical limitations. However, working remotely also presents notable challenges. Many individuals struggle with feelings of isolation and find it difficult to separate professional tasks from personal life when living and working in the same space. Furthermore, effective communication requires reliable internet access and modern collaboration software, which are not universally available. Ultimately, while remote work provides remarkable flexibility, organizations and workers must find sustainable ways to address its social drawbacks to ensure long-term success.','2026-09-15 11:46:06','2026-09-15 11:46:06'),(88,'society','The Rise of Remote Work','B2','In recent years, remote work has transformed the modern workforce significantly. Driven by technological advancements, more companies now allow employees to complete their daily tasks away from traditional offices. This shift offers numerous advantages, such as saving commuting time and reducing urban traffic congestion. Employees often report a better work-life balance because they can manage their schedules more flexibly. However, working from home also presents challenges. Many individuals experience feelings of isolation due to a lack of face-to-face interaction with colleagues. Additionally, separating personal life from professional duties can become difficult when living spaces double as workspaces. To address these issues, many organizations are adopting a hybrid model. This approach combines remote days with mandatory office attendance, allowing staff members to enjoy the flexibility of working from home while maintaining strong team collaboration. Ultimately, the future of employment seems to rely heavily on adaptability.','2026-09-15 11:46:14','2026-09-15 11:46:14'),(89,'society','The Impact of Remote Work on Modern Cities','B2','The rise of remote work has significantly transformed modern urban societies. Over the past few years, thousands of office employees have shifted from traditional commuting to working from home. This flexibility has allowed many city residents to relocate to suburban or rural areas where housing is more affordable and living spaces are larger. Consequently, downtown areas that once bustled with daily commuters are now experiencing economic shifts. Local businesses such as cafes, sandwich shops, and public transport systems that heavily relied on office workers have seen a sharp decline in daily revenue. On the positive hand, neighborhood stores in residential areas are thriving as people stay close to home during the workday. City planners are now forced to rethink urban spaces, suggesting that empty office buildings should be converted into residential apartments. While remote work offers undeniable benefits for individual work-life balance, it challenges the traditional economic ecosystem of city centers. Urban authorities must adapt quickly to these changing patterns to ensure the long-term sustainability and vitality of metropolitan areas.','2026-09-15 11:46:22','2026-09-15 11:46:22'),(90,'society','The Rise of Remote Work','B2','In recent years, remote work has transformed the modern workforce. Driven by technological advancements, many companies now allow employees to complete their tasks from home. This shift offers numerous benefits, including a better work-life balance and the elimination of daily commuting stress. Employees no longer spend hours trapped in traffic, which significantly boosts their daily productivity and overall job satisfaction. Furthermore, businesses can reduce their operational expenses by maintaining smaller physical offices. However, remote working is not without its challenges. Some workers report feeling isolated from their colleagues, as digital communication lacks the warmth of face-to-face interactions. Additionally, maintaining clear boundaries between professional duties and personal life can be difficult when living and working in the same environment. Despite these obstacles, the trend of working remotely continues to grow, permanently changing how society views traditional office employment.','2026-09-15 11:46:30','2026-09-15 11:46:30'),(91,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes where everyday devices are connected to the internet. Homeowners can now control lighting, security systems, and heating remotely using their smartphones. This automation offers significant benefits, particularly in energy efficiency. Smart thermostats, for instance, learn household routines and adjust temperatures automatically to reduce electricity waste. Furthermore, voice-activated assistants allow users to manage their schedules, play music, and check the weather simply by speaking. Despite these advantages, smart home technology presents certain challenges. Privacy and cybersecurity are major concerns, as connected devices can potentially be hacked by malicious actors. Additionally, the high initial cost of purchasing and installing these advanced systems makes them less accessible for budget-conscious families. Nevertheless, market demand continues to grow steadily as manufacturers improve security features and make devices more affordable.','2026-09-15 11:46:39','2026-09-15 11:46:39'),(92,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed how we live, especially through the rapid growth of smart home devices. Today, homeowners can easily control lighting, heating, and security systems using their smartphones or voice-activated assistants. These intelligent systems are designed to improve energy efficiency and provide greater convenience for residents. For instance, smart thermostats can automatically learn household routines and adjust temperatures to reduce electricity waste. Meanwhile, advanced security cameras allow users to monitor their properties remotely while they are away at work or on vacation. Despite these clear benefits, several challenges remain. Privacy concerns are increasing as smart devices collect massive amounts of personal data daily. Additionally, high installation costs can prevent many families from adopting these new technologies. However, as manufacturing processes improve, prices are expected to decrease significantly in the coming years, making smart homes accessible to a wider audience worldwide.','2026-09-15 11:46:47','2026-09-15 11:46:47'),(93,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes where everyday devices are connected to the internet. Homeowners can now control their lighting, heating, and security systems remotely using smartphones or voice assistants. For instance, smart thermostats learn user preferences over time and adjust temperatures automatically to save energy. Furthermore, advanced security cameras provide real-time alerts and video feeds directly to the owner\'s mobile device, enhancing overall household safety. Despite these benefits, critics argue that increased connectivity poses potential privacy risks. Hackers might target vulnerable home networks to gain unauthorized access to personal data. Therefore, cybersecurity experts strongly advise users to update their passwords regularly and use encrypted connections to protect their smart devices from malicious attacks.','2026-09-15 11:46:54','2026-09-15 11:46:54'),(94,'technology','The Rise of Smart Homes','B2','Modern technology has transformed our living spaces into smart homes. Devices such as smart thermostats, automated lighting systems, and voice-activated assistants are becoming increasingly common in households around the world. These innovations primarily aim to improve energy efficiency, enhance home security, and provide greater convenience for residents. For instance, smart thermostats can learn a homeowner\'s daily schedule and adjust the temperature automatically, which significantly reduces electricity bills. Meanwhile, advanced security cameras allow owners to monitor their property remotely using a smartphone application. Despite these clear benefits, the widespread adoption of smart home technology also presents notable challenges. Cybersecurity is a major concern, as connected devices can sometimes be vulnerable to hacking. Furthermore, the high initial cost of purchasing and installing these sophisticated gadgets can deter budget-conscious consumers. Nevertheless, as technology continues to evolve, smart homes are expected to become an ordinary standard of modern living rather than a luxury.','2026-09-15 11:47:02','2026-09-15 11:47:02'),(95,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','Every Saturday, Anna wakes up early at seven o\'clock. She likes to drink a warm cup of coffee and eat some toast with butter for breakfast. After breakfast, she cleans her small apartment and listens to her favorite music. In the afternoon, Anna usually goes to the local supermarket to buy fresh vegetables, milk, and apples. She loves cooking dinner for herself and her roommate in the evening. On Sundays, she prefers to relax in the park, read interesting books, and sometimes meet her friends at a coffee shop. Anna enjoys her peaceful weekend very much because it helps her prepare for a busy work week.','2026-09-15 11:57:19','2026-09-15 11:57:19'),(96,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','Every Saturday, I wake up at 8 o\'clock in the morning. First, I make a cup of hot coffee and eat some toast with butter for breakfast. Then, I clean my small apartment and wash my clothes. In the afternoon, I usually go to the local supermarket to buy fresh vegetables, milk, and eggs for the coming week. Walking to the market helps me stay active and healthy. When I return home, I listen to some relaxing music and read my favorite book. On Sunday, I like to visit my parents who live in a quiet neighborhood near the city center. We cook lunch together and talk about our week. Sometimes we walk in the nearby park if the weather is nice. My weekend routine is simple, but it makes me feel happy and ready for a busy Monday.','2026-09-15 11:57:40','2026-09-15 11:57:40'),(97,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','My name is Linh. Today is Saturday, and the weather is very nice and sunny. I go to the big park near my house with my little brother, Nam. We walk to the park at nine o\'clock in the morning. Many people are at the park today. Some children play football on the green grass. An old man sits on a brown bench and reads a thick book. Nam and I bring a red ball and some snacks. We play catch with the ball for one hour. After that, we eat some sweet apples and drink fresh water. We are very happy. We go home at eleven o\'clock because we need to eat lunch with our parents.','2026-09-15 23:41:08','2026-09-15 23:41:08'),(98,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','My name is Anna and I love weekends. Every Saturday, I wake up at 8 o\'clock in the morning. First, I make a cup of hot coffee and eat a healthy breakfast with my family. We usually have eggs and fresh fruit. After breakfast, I clean my house and wash the dirty clothes. In the afternoon, I go to the local supermarket to buy food for the week. I like to buy fresh vegetables, milk, and bread. On Sunday, I like to relax. I read a good book in my small garden and listen to music. Sometimes, my friends come to my house for dinner. We cook pasta together and talk about our week. Weekends are always short, but they make me very happy and ready for work on Monday.','2026-09-15 23:41:15','2026-09-15 23:41:15'),(99,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','Every Saturday morning, Anna goes to the green park near her house. She likes to walk on the soft grass and listen to the birds sing. The park has many tall trees and colorful flowers like red roses and yellow sunflowers. Anna usually wears her comfortable blue shoes and takes a small brown bag with water and an apple. Sometimes, she meets her friend Ben at the park. They sit on a wooden bench and talk about their week. Around twelve o\'clock, Anna walks back home for lunch. She always feels happy and relaxed after her morning walk in the park.','2026-09-15 23:41:38','2026-09-15 23:41:38'),(100,'general','My Favorite Weekend Routine','A1','My name is Anna, and I live in a small apartment in the city. Every weekend, I have a simple routine that makes me very happy. On Saturday morning, I wake up at eight o\'clock and make a warm cup of coffee. Then, I go to the local market to buy fresh vegetables and sweet fruits. The market is very busy and colorful. In the afternoon, I usually clean my living room and listen to my favorite jazz music. Sometimes, my best friend Linh comes to visit me, and we bake chocolate cookies together. On Sunday, I like to relax quietly. I spend two hours reading an interesting book on my comfortable sofa in the evening. This weekend routine helps me forget all the stress from work and gives me energy for the new week.','2026-09-17 03:28:37','2026-09-17 03:28:37'),(101,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','Every Saturday morning, Anna goes to the green park near her house. She likes to walk on the soft grass and listen to the birds sing. The park has many tall trees and colorful flowers like red roses and yellow sunflowers. Anna usually wears a comfortable blue hat and brings a small bottle of cold water with her. Sometimes, she sits on a wooden bench to read her favorite book. At twelve o\'clock, she walks back home to eat lunch with her family. Anna loves the park because it is very quiet and peaceful.','2026-09-17 03:29:51','2026-09-17 03:29:51'),(102,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','My name is Linh. Every Sunday, I go to the big park near my house with my family. The park has many tall green trees and a small blue lake. My father likes to read a newspaper on the wooden bench under a tree. My mother walks on the grass and listens to music with her headphones. My little brother likes to play football with his friends near the playground. I love taking pictures of colorful flowers and cute birds with my small camera. In the afternoon, we always eat sandwiches and drink cold water together. We usually go home at five o\'clock in the evening because it starts to get dark. I am always happy on Sundays.','2026-09-17 03:31:03','2026-09-17 03:31:03'),(103,'general','A Day at the Park','A1','My name is Linh. Today is Saturday, and the weather is very nice and sunny. I go to the big park near my house with my younger brother, Nam. We walk to the park at nine o\'clock in the morning. Many people are at the park today. Some children are playing football on the green grass. An old man is sitting on a wooden bench and reading a book. My brother Nam loves animals, so he buys some bread to feed the brown ducks in the small pond. I bring my pink camera and take many pictures of flowers and trees. We feel very happy and relaxed. We walk back home at eleven o\'clock because we are hungry and want to eat lunch.','2026-09-17 03:31:43','2026-09-17 03:31:43'),(104,'general','The Benefits of Walking Daily','B1','Walking is one of the easiest and cheapest ways to improve your physical and mental health. You do not need expensive gym equipment or a special training program to start. All you need is a comfortable pair of shoes and a little bit of free time every day. Taking a brisk walk for just thirty minutes daily can strengthen your heart, reduce stress levels, and help you maintain a healthy weight. Many people prefer to walk in the morning before they go to work because it gives them extra energy for the day. Others like to walk in the evening to relax after a long and tiring workday. Furthermore, walking in local parks allows you to enjoy nature and fresh air, which is great for clearing your mind. If you are busy, you can simply walk to the grocery store instead of driving your car. Small changes in your daily routine can lead to big improvements in your overall well-being over time.','2026-09-20 21:30:00','2026-09-20 21:30:00');
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `reading_passages` ENABLE KEYS */;
/*!40101 SET @saved_cs_client     = @@character_set_client */;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = utf8 */;
CREATE TABLE `reading_questions` (
  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `passage_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL,
  `type` varchar(10) NOT NULL,
  `question` text NOT NULL,
  `options` longtext CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_bin DEFAULT NULL CHECK (json_valid(`options`)),
  `correct_answer` text NOT NULL,
  `order` int(10) unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `updated_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  KEY `reading_questions_passage_id_foreign` (`passage_id`),
  CONSTRAINT `reading_questions_passage_id_foreign` FOREIGN KEY (`passage_id`) REFERENCES `reading_passages` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE
) ENGINE=InnoDB AUTO_INCREMENT=521 DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;
/*!40101 SET character_set_client = @saved_cs_client */;

/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `reading_questions` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `reading_questions` VALUES (1,1,'fill','What kind of costs can businesses reduce by maintaining smaller physical office spaces?','[]','[\"overhead costs\"]',0,'2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(2,1,'boolean','Allowing employees to work from home decreases overall productivity.','[]','[\"False\"]',1,'2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(3,1,'mcq','What do successful organizations invest in to overcome communication hurdles with remote teams?','[\"Advanced collaboration tools\",\"Larger physical office spaces\",\"Temporary marketing trends\",\"Traditional communication methods\"]','[\"Advanced collaboration tools\"]',2,'2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(4,1,'multi','According to the text, what are some benefits of remote work for businesses?','[\"Increases overall productivity\",\"Boosts job satisfaction\",\"Eliminates all management challenges\",\"Reduces overhead costs\"]','[\"Increases overall productivity\",\"Boosts job satisfaction\",\"Reduces overhead costs\"]',3,'2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(5,1,'fill','What has flexibility become a key factor in within a competitive job market?','[]','[\"attracting top talent\"]',4,'2026-09-14 23:36:06','2026-09-14 23:36:06'),(6,2,'fill','Complete the phrase based on the text: remote work has evolved from a temporary solution into a permanent business strategy for many companies, offering reduced operational costs for office space and increased employee satisfaction due to better _________.','[]','[\"work-life balance\"]',0,'2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(7,2,'boolean','True or False: Employers hiring new staff through remote work are no longer restricted by geographic boundaries.','[]','[\"True\"]',1,'2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(8,2,'mcq','What are companies heavily investing in to overcome remote team challenges?','[\"Traditional office buildings\",\"Digital collaboration tools\",\"Geographic expansion\",\"Employee relocation\"]','[\"Digital collaboration tools\"]',2,'2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(9,2,'multi','Which of the following are mentioned as benefits of remote work in the text? (Choose all that apply)','[\"Reduced operational costs for office space\",\"Increased employee satisfaction\",\"Elimination of all management challenges\",\"A broader talent pool\",\"Guaranteed higher daily profits\"]','[\"Reduced operational costs for office space\",\"Increased employee satisfaction\",\"A broader talent pool\"]',3,'2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(10,2,'fill','Complete the sentence based on the text: Businesses that successfully balance flexibility with _________ will thrive in this new environment.','[]','[\"accountability\"]',4,'2026-09-14 23:36:11','2026-09-14 23:36:11'),(11,3,'fill','Complete the sentence with an exact word or phrase from the text: Companies of all sizes are discovering that employees can maintain high levels of productivity without being physically present in a traditional ____________.','[]','[\"office environment\"]',0,'2026-09-14 23:36:32','2026-09-14 23:36:32'),(12,3,'boolean','True or False: Managing a remote workforce eliminates all operational challenges for business leaders.','[]','[\"False\"]',1,'2026-09-14 23:36:32','2026-09-14 23:36:32'),(13,3,'mcq','What is one main advantage of remote work mentioned in the text?','[\"Eliminating the need for data security\",\"Reduced overhead costs for office space\",\"Guaranteed face-to-face interactions\",\"Lowering employee productivity levels\"]','[\"Reduced overhead costs for office space\"]',2,'2026-09-14 23:36:32','2026-09-14 23:36:32'),(14,3,'multi','Which two challenges of managing a remote workforce are mentioned in the text? (Select two)','[\"Maintaining strong communication\",\"Building team cohesion\",\"Decreasing employee flexibility\",\"Eliminating top talent from a global labor pool\"]','[\"Maintaining strong communication\",\"Building team cohesion\"]',3,'2026-09-14 23:36:32','2026-09-14 