,'Select all coordinating conjunctions that are part of the FANBOYS acronym mentioned in the material.','[\"because\",\"and\",\"yet\",\"although\",\"so\"]','[\"and\",\"yet\",\"so\"]',18,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(545,16,'mcq','Select the correct coordinating conjunction from the FANBOYS acronym to show contrast:','[\"and\",\"but\",\"so\",\"for\"]','[\"but\"]',19,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(546,16,'mcq','Select the correct quantifier for an affirmative sentence with an uncountable noun: \'I have ___ money left in my wallet.\'','[\"many\",\"few\",\"a lot of\",\"these\"]','[\"a lot of\"]',20,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(547,16,'mcq','Choose the correct verb form: \'She enjoys ___ pop music in her free time.\'','[\"listen\",\"to listen\",\"listening\",\"listened\"]','[\"listening\"]',21,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(548,16,'fill','The children baked a cake all by ___ for their mother\'s birthday.','[]','[\"themselves\"]',22,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(549,16,'mcq','Identify the correct interrogative pronoun for the question: \'___ jacket is this on the chair?\'','[\"Who\",\"Whom\",\"Whose\",\"Which\"]','[\"Whose\"]',23,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(550,16,'fill','This blue jacket is mine, but that red one is ___.','[]','[\"yours\"]',24,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(551,16,'fill','There are very ___ books left on the library shelf; we need to buy more.','[]','[\"few\"]',25,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(552,16,'fill','She packed her clothes into a heavy ___ leather suitcase.','[]','[\"brown\"]',26,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(553,16,'fill','He arrived ___ Monday morning for the important meeting.','[]','[\"on\"]',27,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(554,16,'mcq','Which of the following sentences features a linking verb?','[\"She runs in the park every morning.\",\"The warm biscuit tastes sweet.\",\"He writes letters to his friends.\",\"They cooked dinner in the kitchen.\"]','[\"The warm biscuit tastes sweet.\"]',28,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(555,16,'fill','The two friends always help ___ when they face difficult problems.','[]','[\"each other\"]',29,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(556,16,'fill','Jane was holding an apple in her hand. She gave ___ to her little brother.','[]','[\"it\"]',30,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(557,16,'multi','Select all modal verbs from the list that express advice or obligation.','[\"should\",\"might\",\"must\",\"can\",\"ought to\"]','[\"should\",\"must\",\"ought to\"]',31,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(558,16,'multi','Select all words from the options that are classified as proper nouns in English grammar.','[\"Paris\",\"camera\",\"John\",\"river\",\"Canon\"]','[\"Paris\",\"John\",\"Canon\"]',32,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(559,16,'fill','My sister bought ___ new camera yesterday.','[]','[\"a\"]',33,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(560,16,'fill','Although it was raining heavily, ___ he still walked to school.','[]','[\"yet\"]',34,'2026-09-16 12:27:44','2026-09-16 12:27:44'),(596,18,'mcq','Choose the correct preposition of time for dates: \'His birthday is ___ May 5th.\'','[\"in\",\"at\",\"on\",\"by\"]','[\"on\"]',0,'2026-09-20 21:49:23','2026-09-20 21:49:23'),(597,18,'multi','Select all verbs from the reference material that are followed ONLY by a gerund:','[\"enjoy\",\"want\",\"avoid\",\"finish\",\"decide\"]','[\"enjoy\",\"avoid\",\"finish\"]',1,'2026-09-20 21:49:23','2026-09-20 21:49:23'),(598,18,'fill','Although the test was difficult, ___ student passed it successfully.','[]','[\"every\"]',2,'2026-09-20 21:49:23','2026-09-20 21:49:23'),(599,18,'multi','Select all adverbs of frequency from the following list:','[\"always\",\"carefully\",\"often\",\"never\",\"yesterday\"]','[\"always\",\"often\",\"never\"]',3,'2026-09-20 21:49:23','2026-09-20 21:49:2