 is essential that he arrived on time.\",\"It is essential that he will arrive on time.\"]','[\"It is essential that he arrive on time.\"]',4,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(216,7,'mcq','Select the correct sentence for a Type 0 Conditional.','[\"If you heat metal, it expands.\",\"If you heat metal, it will expand.\",\"If you heat metal, it would expand.\",\"If you heat metal, it expanded.\"]','[\"If you heat metal, it expands.\"]',5,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(217,7,'mcq','Which option correctly uses a Causative verb structure (have/get something done)?','[\"I had my hair cut yesterday.\",\"I cut my hair by myself yesterday.\",\"I had cut my hair yesterday.\",\"I got cutting my hair yesterday.\"]','[\"I had my hair cut yesterday.\"]',6,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(218,7,'fill','This smartphone is not ___ expensive as the newest model.','[]','[\"as\"]',7,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(219,7,'fill','Never ___ I witnessed such a magnificent performance.','[]','[\"have\"]',8,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(220,7,'fill','The report ___ finished by the secretary yesterday.','[]','[\"was\"]',9,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(221,7,'fill','This is ___ most interesting movie I have ever watched.','[]','[\"the\"]',10,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(222,7,'mcq','Which sentence correctly expresses a past regret using a Wish clause?','[\"I wish I had studied harder for the final test.\",\"I wish I studied harder for the final test.\",\"I wish I would study harder for the final test.\",\"I wish I have studied harder for the final test.\"]','[\"I wish I had studied harder for the final test.\"]',11,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(223,7,'mcq','Choose the correctly inverted sentence using \'No sooner\'.','[\"No sooner had he arrived than the phone rang.\",\"No sooner he had arrived than the phone rang.\",\"No sooner did he arrive when the phone rang.\",\"No sooner has he arrived than the phone rang.\"]','[\"No sooner had he arrived than the phone rang.\"]',12,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(224,7,'fill','If you freeze water, it ___ into ice.','[]','[\"turns\"]',13,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(225,7,'fill','It was my brother ___ fixed the broken bicycle.','[]','[\"who\"]',14,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(226,7,'fill','I wish I ___ a larger apartment in the city center.','[]','[\"had\"]',15,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(227,7,'mcq','Select the correct Passive Voice transformation of: \'The mechanic is repairing my car.\'','[\"My car is being repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car was repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car is repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car has been repaired by the mechanic.\"]','[\"My car is being repaired by the mechanic.\"]',16,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(228,7,'mcq','Which sentence correctly uses a Defining Relative Clause?','[\"The engineer who designed this bridge is brilliant.\",\"The engineer, who designed this bridge, is brilliant.\",\"The engineer which designed this bridge is brilliant.\",\"The engineer, that designed this bridge, is brilliant.\"]','[\"The engineer who designed this bridge is brilliant.\"]',17,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(229,7,'multi','Select all statements that correctly describe Noun Clauses based on the reference material.','[\"They function as a noun (subject, object, or complement).\",\"They usually start with \'that\', \'if\\/whether\', or a wh-word.\",\"They can act as the subject of a sentence.\",\"They must always be enclosed in commas like non-defining clauses.\",\"They can act as the object of a sentence.\"]','[\"They function as a noun (subject, object, or complement).\",\"They usually start with \'that\', \'if\\/whether\', or a wh-word.\",\"They can act as the subject of a sentence.\",\"They can act as the object of a sentence.\"]',18,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(230,7,'multi','Identify all sentences that use Inversion triggered by negative or limiting adverbials.','[\"Never have I seen such a stunning sunset.\",\"Not only did she win the prize, but she also set a record.\",\"Hardly had I opened the door when the cat ran out.\",\"I have never seen such a stunning sunset.\",\"Little did he know about the surprise party.\"]','[\"Never have I seen such a stunning sunset.\",\"Not only did she win the prize, but she also set a record.\",\"Hardly had I opened the door when the cat ran out.\",\"Little did he know about the surprise party.\"]',19,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(231,7,'fill','If she studies hard tonight, she ___ pass the exam tomorrow.','[]','[\"will\"]',20,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(232,7,'fill','___ the report carefully before submitting it.','[]','[\"Read\"]',21,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(233,7,'mcq','Which sentence correctly uses the comparative form of a long adjective?','[\"This laptop is more expensive than that one.\",\"This laptop is expensiver than that one.\",\"This laptop is the most expensive than that one.\",\"This laptop is more expensiver than that one.\"]','[\"This laptop is more expensive than that one.\"]',22,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(234,7,'multi','Which of the following examples correctly illustrate Participle Clauses from the reference material?','[\"The woman standing by the door is my aunt.\",\"The letter written in French was hard to read.\",\"Having finished his homework, he went out to play.\",\"The man who is standing by the door is my aunt.\",\"If he finishes his homework, he will go out.\"]','[\"The woman standing by the door is my aunt.\",\"The letter written in French was hard to read.\",\"Having finished his homework, he went out to play.\"]',23,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(235,7,'multi','Which of the following sentences correctly demonstrate the Superlative form?','[\"This is the most exciting movie of the year.\",\"She is the smart student in the class.\",\"Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world.\",\"That building is taller than this one.\",\"He runs the fastest of all competitors.\"]','[\"This is the most exciting movie of the year.\",\"Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world.\",\"He runs the fastest of all competitors.\"]',24,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(236,7,'mcq','Select the correct sentence using a Participle Clause (active meaning with -ing).','[\"The man standing by the counter is the manager.\",\"The man stood by the counter is the manager.\",\"The man stand by the counter is the manager.\",\"The man having stand by the counter is the manager.\"]','[\"The man standing by the counter is the manager.\"]',25,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(237,7,'mcq','Select the correct cleft sentence emphasizing the object.','[\"It was the blue dress that she bought yesterday.\",\"It was she who bought the blue dress yesterday.\",\"What she bought yesterday was the blue dress.\",\"All of the above are correct cleft structures.\"]','[\"All of the above are correct cleft structures.\"]',26,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(238,7,'fill','If I were the manager, I ___ hire more staff.','[]','[\"would\"]',27,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(239,7,'mcq','Choose the correct Superlative form for a short adjective.','[\"She is the tallest girl in her class.\",\"She is taller girl in her class.\",\"She is the most tall girl in her class.\",\"She is tallest girl in her class.\"]','[\"She is the tallest girl in her class.\"]',28,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(240,7,'multi','Which of the following are valid Wish Clause structures covered in the material?','[\"Wish + past simple for present situations\",\"Wish + past perfect for past regrets\",\"Wish + would + V for annoyance about someone else\'s habit\",\"Wish + present simple for future plans\",\"Wish + will + V for instant decisions\"]','[\"Wish + past simple for present situations\",\"Wish + past perfect for past regrets\",\"Wish + would + V for annoyance about someone else\'s habit\"]',29,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(241,7,'mcq','Identify the correct Type 3 Conditional sentence.','[\"If she had taken the bus, she wouldn\'t have been late.\",\"If she took the bus, she wouldn\'t be late.\",\"If she takes the bus, she won\'t be late.\",\"If she had taken the bus, she wouldn\'t be late.\"]','[\"If she had taken the bus, she wouldn\'t have been late.\"]',30,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(242,7,'fill','I must get my laptop ___ before the presentation.','[]','[\"repaired\"]',31,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(243,7,'mcq','Choose the correct Reported Speech for: \'I am leaving now,\' she said.','[\"She said that she was leaving then.\",\"She said that she is leaving now.\",\"She said that she left then.\",\"She said that she will leave now.\"]','[\"She said that she was leaving then.\"]',32,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(244,7,'fill','The manager insisted that every employee ___ present at the meeting.','[]','[\"be\"]',33,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(245,7,'multi','Select all sentences that are examples of Type 1 Conditionals.','[\"If it rains tomorrow, we will cancel the trip.\",\"If you mix red and blue, you get purple.\",\"If she studies hard, she will pass the test.\",\"If I were you, I would accept the job.\",\"If they arrive early, we will start the meeting.\"]','[\"If it rains tomorrow, we will cancel the trip.\",\"If she studies hard, she will pass the test.\",\"If they arrive early, we will start the meeting.\"]',34,'2026-09-16 12:22:48','2026-09-16 12:22:48'),(246,8,'mcq','Which sentence uses proper inversion after a negative adverbial?','[\"Hardly I had sat down when the lights went out.\",\"Hardly had I sat down when the lights went out.\",\"Never I have seen such a breathtaking view.\",\"Not only she passed the exam, but she also won a prize.\"]','[\"Hardly had I sat down when the lights went out.\"]',0,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(247,8,'fill','___ finished her homework, Anna went out to meet her friends.','[]','[\"Having\"]',1,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(248,8,'fill','___ the window before you leave the room.','[]','[\"Close\"]',2,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(249,8,'mcq','Choose the correct Type 2 Conditional sentence for an unreal present situation.','[\"If I have a million dollars, I will buy a boat.\",\"If I had a million dollars, I would buy a boat.\",\"If I had had a million dollars, I would buy a boat.\",\"If I have a million dollars, I would buy a boat.\"]','[\"If I had a million dollars, I would buy a boat.\"]',3,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(250,8,'fill','The report must ___ finished before tomorrow morning.','[]','[\"be\"]',4,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(251,8,'mcq','Identify the correct mixed conditional sentence.','[\"If she had taken the course last year, she will have a better job now.\",\"If she took the course last year, she would have a better job now.\",\"If she had taken the course last year, she would be a manager now.\",\"If she has taken the course last year, she would be a manager now.\"]','[\"If she had taken the course last year, she would be a manager now.\"]',5,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(252,8,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use the Subjunctive mood after demanding or essential expressions.','[\"It is essential that he be informed immediately.\",\"She demanded that the money be returned at once.\",\"I suggested that she goes to the doctor.\",\"It is important that everyone arrive on time.\",\"He insisted that he was innocent.\"]','[\"It is essential that he be informed immediately.\",\"She demanded that the money be returned at once.\",\"It is important that everyone arrive on time.\"]',6,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(253,8,'fill','I wish I ___ how to swim when I was a child.','[]','[\"had known\"]',7,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(254,8,'fill','I don\'t remember where I ___ my keys.','[]','[\"put\"]',8,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(255,8,'multi','Select all sentences that use the Causative structure (have/get something done).','[\"I had my hair cut yesterday.\",\"She cut her hair by herself last week.\",\"We are going to get our windows cleaned.\",\"He had his assistant type the report.\",\"They got their house painted last month.\"]','[\"I had my hair cut yesterday.\",\"We are going to get our windows cleaned.\",\"They got their house painted last month.\"]',9,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(256,8,'fill','My new computer is not ___ fast as my old one.','[]','[\"so\"]',10,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(257,8,'multi','Select all sentences that contain a Noun Clause acting as a subject, object, or complement.','[\"What you just said made everyone laugh.\",\"The man who lives next door is a pilot.\",\"I wonder whether she will come to the party.\",\"The problem is that we have run out of time.\",\"Running every morning is good for your health.\"]','[\"What you just said made everyone laugh.\",\"I wonder whether she will come to the party.\",\"The problem is that we have run out of time.\"]',11,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(258,8,'mcq','Choose the correct passive voice form of: \'The mechanic is repairing my car.\'','[\"My car is repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car was being repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car is being repaired by the mechanic.\",\"My car has been repaired by the mechanic.\"]','[\"My car is being repaired by the mechanic.\"]',12,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(259,8,'mcq','Which of these is a correct negative imperative sentence?','[\"Not touch that wire.\",\"Don\'t you touch that wire.\",\"Don\'t touch that wire.\",\"You don\'t touch that wire.\"]','[\"Don\'t touch that wire.\"]',13,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(260,8,'fill','Tomorrow, I am going to have my car ___ by a professional mechanic.','[]','[\"repaired\"]',14,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(261,8,'mcq','Convert to reported speech: \'I will finish the report tomorrow,\' said Tom.','[\"Tom said that he will finish the report tomorrow.\",\"Tom said that he would finish the report the next day.\",\"Tom told that he finishes the report tomorrow.\",\"Tom said that he finished the report the next day.\"]','[\"Tom said that he would finish the report the next day.\"]',15,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(262,8,'fill','She told me that she ___ busy the day before.','[]','[\"was\"]',16,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(263,8,'mcq','Which sentence uses a participle clause to replace a relative clause correctly?','[\"The boy played in the garden is my nephew.\",\"The boy playing in the garden is my nephew.\",\"The boy plays in the garden is my nephew.\",\"The boy played in the garden, he is my nephew.\"]','[\"The boy playing in the garden is my nephew.\"]',17,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(264,8,'fill','It was my brother ___ helped me fix my bicycle.','[]','[\"who\"]',18,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(265,8,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use the Superlative form.','[\"This is the most interesting book I have ever read.\",\"She is the tallest student in our class.\",\"He is the most fast runner on the team.\",\"This is the more expensive restaurant in town.\",\"That was the worst movie of the year.\"]','[\"This is the most interesting book I have ever read.\",\"She is the tallest student in our class.\",\"That was the worst movie of the year.\"]',19,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(266,8,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly demonstrate Inversion triggered by negative adverbials.','[\"Never have I witnessed such a generous act.\",\"Rarely do they visit their hometown.\",\"Not only did she win the competition, but she also broke a record.\",\"Seldom I have seen such terrible weather.\",\"No sooner had the concert started than the lights went out.\"]','[\"Never have I witnessed such a generous act.\",\"Rarely do they visit their hometown.\",\"Not only did she win the competition, but she also broke a record.\",\"No sooner had the concert started than the lights went out.\"]',20,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(267,8,'mcq','What does the sentence \'I had my roof fixed yesterday\' mean?','[\"I fixed the roof myself yesterday.\",\"I arranged for someone else to fix my roof yesterday.\",\"Somebody forced me to fix the roof yesterday.\",\"I was fixing the roof when someone interrupted me.\"]','[\"I arranged for someone else to fix my roof yesterday.\"]',21,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(268,8,'mcq','Choose the cleft sentence that emphasizes the action or need.','[\"It was the manager who approved the budget.\",\"What we need right now is more time.\",\"It is English grammar that I find most challenging.\",\"What surprised me was her sudden resignation.\"]','[\"What we need right now is more time.\"]',22,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(269,8,'fill','If you freeze water, it ___ into ice.','[]','[\"turns\"]',23,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(270,8,'multi','Select all sentences that are examples of Type 2 Conditionals.','[\"If I were you, I would accept the job offer.\",\"If it rains tomorrow, we will cancel the trip.\",\"If she spoke French fluently, she would get the position.\",\"If you heat ice, it melts.\",\"If I had a private jet, I would fly everywhere.\"]','[\"If I were you, I would accept the job offer.\",\"If she spoke French fluently, she would get the position.\",\"If I had a private jet, I would fly everywhere.\"]',24,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(271,8,'fill','Mount Everest is ___ highest mountain in the world.','[]','[\"the\"]',25,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(272,8,'mcq','Choose the sentence with a correct non-defining relative clause.','[\"My uncle who lives in Paris is an artist.\",\"My uncle, who lives in Paris, is an artist.\",\"My uncle, that lives in Paris, is an artist.\",\"My uncle who, lives in Paris, is an artist.\"]','[\"My uncle, who lives in Paris, is an artist.\"]',26,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(273,8,'fill','Little ___ he know that a surprise party was waiting for him.','[]','[\"did\"]',27,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(274,8,'mcq','Choose the correct Type 1 Conditional sentence.','[\"If you study hard, you will pass the exam.\",\"If you study hard, you pass the exam.\",\"If you studied hard, you will pass the exam.\",\"If you study hard, you would pass the exam.\"]','[\"If you study hard, you will pass the exam.\"]',28,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(275,8,'mcq','Identify the correct subjunctive sentence.','[\"The doctor recommended that he stays in bed.\",\"The doctor recommended that he staying in bed.\",\"The doctor recommended that he stay in bed.\",\"The doctor recommended him staying in bed.\"]','[\"The doctor recommended that he stay in bed.\"]',29,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(276,8,'mcq','Which sentence correctly uses the comparative form of adjectives?','[\"This exercise is more easy than the last one.\",\"Your house is much bigger than mine.\",\"She is the taller girl in the classroom.\",\"This problem is more hard than that one.\"]','[\"Your house is much bigger than mine.\"]',30,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(277,8,'fill','The manager insisted that every employee ___ present at the meeting.','[]','[\"be\"]',31,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(278,8,'mcq','Which wish clause expresses an annoying habit of another person?','[\"I wish I had a bigger house.\",\"I wish I had studied harder for the test.\",\"I wish it would stop raining.\",\"I wish she was here.\"]','[\"I wish it would stop raining.\"]',32,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(279,8,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use Participle Clauses.','[\"Written in clear English, the manual was easy to understand.\",\"Having completed the assignment, Mark went to sleep.\",\"The girl sings on the stage is my sister.\",\"Built in the 19th century, the castle attracts many tourists.\",\"Walking down the street, a tree fell on his car.\"]','[\"Written in clear English, the manual was easy to understand.\",\"Having completed the assignment, Mark went to sleep.\",\"Built in the 19th century, the castle attracts many tourists.\"]',33,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(280,8,'fill','If I had known about the traffic, I ___ taken another route.','[]','[\"would have\"]',34,'2026-09-16 12:23:07','2026-09-16 12:23:07'),(281,9,'fill','Last week, I had my laptop ___ by a professional technician.','[]','[\"repaired\"]',0,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(282,9,'mcq','Which sentence contains a correct non-defining relative clause?','[\"My English teacher who is very friendly gave us no homework.\",\"My English teacher, who is very friendly, gave us no homework.\",\"My English teacher, that is very friendly, gave us no homework.\",\"My English teacher who, is very friendly, gave us no homework.\"]','[\"My English teacher, who is very friendly, gave us no homework.\"]',1,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(283,9,'mcq','Which sentence correctly uses a wish clause to express annoyance about a habit?','[\"I wish you stopped playing loud music.\",\"I wish you would stop playing loud music.\",\"I wish you had stopped playing loud music.\",\"I wish you stop playing loud music.\"]','[\"I wish you would stop playing loud music.\"]',2,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(284,9,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use participle clauses (replacing full clauses with -ing, -ed, or having + V3):','[\"Driven by ambition, he worked day and night.\",