If she had more time, she would learn French.\",\"If they practiced daily, they would improve their skills.\",\"If it rains, we stay inside.\"]','[\"If I were a bird, I would fly across the ocean.\",\"If she had more time, she would learn French.\",\"If they practiced daily, they would improve their skills.\"]',16,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(298,9,'mcq','Select the correct reported speech for: \'I am reading a book,\' he said.','[\"He said that he is reading a book.\",\"He said that he was reading a book.\",\"He said that he has been reading a book.\",\"He said that he will read a book.\"]','[\"He said that he was reading a book.\"]',17,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(299,9,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use subjunctive verbs after demanding or suggesting phrases:','[\"The doctor recommended that he take a week off.\",\"It is important that every student submits their assignment on time.\",\"She demanded that the manager apologize immediately.\",\"I insist that she be invited to the conference.\",\"He suggested that we went out for dinner.\"]','[\"The doctor recommended that he take a week off.\",\"She demanded that the manager apologize immediately.\",\"I insist that she be invited to the conference.\"]',18,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(300,9,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use causative \'have\' or \'get\' something done:','[\"I had my car washed yesterday.\",\"She is getting her hair dyed blonde tomorrow.\",\"They got their roof repaired after the storm.\",\"We had cleaned the house by ourselves.\",\"He got someone fix his computer.\"]','[\"I had my car washed yesterday.\",\"She is getting her hair dyed blonde tomorrow.\",\"They got their roof repaired after the storm.\"]',19,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(301,9,'mcq','Which sentence correctly replaces a relative clause with a present participle (-ing)?','[\"The boy who sits next to me is very smart.\",\"The boy sitting next to me is very smart.\",\"The boy sat next to me is very smart.\",\"The boy sit next to me is very smart.\"]','[\"The boy sitting next to me is very smart.\"]',20,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(302,9,'fill','The manager insisted that every employee ___ present at the meeting tomorrow.','[]','[\"be\"]',21,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(303,9,'mcq','Identify the sentence where a noun clause functions as the subject:','[\"I know what you did last summer.\",\"The problem is that we have no money.\",\"What she told me changed my perspective completely.\",\"She asked me if I liked classical music.\"]','[\"What she told me changed my perspective completely.\"]',22,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(304,9,'fill','___ finished his assignment, Mark went out to play football with his friends.','[]','[\"Having\"]',23,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(305,9,'multi','Select all sentences that correctly use inversion with negative or limiting adverbials:','[\"Hardly had I arrived home when the storm began.\",\"Not only did she win the award, but she also delivered a great speech.\",\"Never I have tasted such delicious food.\",\"No sooner had the movie started than the projector broke.\",\"Little did he know about the surprise party.\"]','[\"Hardly had I arrived home when the storm began.\",\"Not only did she win the award, but she also delivered a great speech.\",\"No sooner had the movie started than the projector broke.\",\"Little did he know about the surprise party.\"]',24,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(306,9,'fill','___ I need right now is a warm cup of coffee and some quiet time.','[]','[\"What\"]',25,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(307,9,'mcq','Select the correct superlative form for a long adjective:','[\"this is the most expensive watch in the shop\",\"this is the more expensive watch in the shop\",\"this is the expensivest watch in the shop\",\"this is most expensive watch in the shop\"]','[\"this is the most expensive watch in the shop\"]',26,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(308,9,'mcq','Choose the correct imperative sentence (negative instruction):','[\"Don\'t to touch the wet paint.\",\"Not touch the wet paint.\",\"Don\'t touch the wet paint.\",\"You don\'t touch the wet paint.\"]','[\"Don\'t touch the wet paint.\"]',27,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(309,9,'fill','The ancient temple ___ built over five hundred years ago.','[]','[\"was\"]',28,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(310,9,'mcq','Choose the correct subjunctive sentence:','[\"It is essential that he arrives on time for the interview.\",\"It is essential that he arrive on time for the interview.\",\"It is essential that he arrived on time for the interview.\",\"It is essential that he is arriving on time for the interview.\"]','[\"It is essential that he arrive on time for the interview.\"]',29,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(311,9,'mcq','Identify the correct mixed conditional sentence (past condition to present result):','[\"If she had taken the medicine yesterday, she would feel better today.\",\"If she took the medicine yesterday, she would feel better today.\",\"If she has taken the medicine yesterday, she feels better today.\",\"If she had taken the medicine yesterday, she will feel better today.\"]','[\"If she had taken the medicine yesterday, she would feel better today.\"]',30,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(312,9,'fill','If you freeze water, it ___ into ice.','[]','[\"turns\"]',31,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(313,9,'mcq','Which sentence demonstrates proper inversion with negative adverbials?','[\"Seldom I have seen such a generous donation.\",\"Seldom have I seen such a generous donation.\",\"Seldom I did see such a generous donation.\",\"Seldom did I have seen such a generous donation.\"]','[\"Seldom have I seen such a generous donation.\"]',32,'2026-09-16 12:23:27','2026-09-16 12:23:27'),(314,9,'fi